1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Se årboka Ætt og Heim 2001 side 97-99 og side 117-128.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5976. Lauritz Knutson Hogganvik was born in ca 1550 in Norway and died in 1627 in Hogganvik, Vikedal, Norway 530 aged 97. 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: Laurits* KNUTSSON Hogganvik was born before 1570 in Norway. He died in 1625 in Hogganvik farm #69, Vikedal, Rogaland, Norway. Laurits Knutsson was the lensmann in Vikedal skiprede from 1591 until 1625. He also repre
2 CONC sented Vikedal at the royal coronations of 1591 and 1610. Laurits leased the entire Hogganvik farm of 21/2 laup smør and 1/2 pund grain. He was also a considerable landowner. In 1610, Laurits owned property worth about 31/2 laup s
2 CONC mør. By 1617, this had increased to 6 laupar 12 mark smør. Since his personally owned property was listed as 3 laupar smør in 1624, it is probable that his first wife brought at least 3 laupar as an inheritance and that she died s
2 CONC ometime between 1617 and 1624. Her property would probably have been divided among their children following her death. Laurits was also named as the owner of Sandvik sawmill in 1614 and the Hogganvik sawmill in 1618. He was defini
2 CONC tely involved in the timber trade with Scottish merchants. In 1618, Laurits was fined 331/2 dalar for selling 5 oak trees to the Scots in violation of a royal edict. Oak was supposed to be used only to build ships for the royal fl
2 CONC eet. Although Laurits was obviously a very wealthy man and prominent citizen of Vikedal, his origins are relatively vague. There has been much speculation among genealogists about his ancestry, but no one has been able to conclusi
2 CONC vely identify his parents. But his two wives were of very high social status and his children all married into prominent Ryfylke families. Laurits, himself, must have come from a wealthy, upper-class family.
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars (Laurits) var lensmann i Vikedal 1591-1625. Han var truleg gift med ei dotter eller dotterdotter av Sevat Oddson Skiftun. Ikring 1617 blei han gift for andre gong, med Katrine Johannesdtr., enkje etter presten i Rennesøy, Ras
2 CONC mus Olson. Han hadde 4 barn i det fyrste ekteskapet. [Magnus Våge: Auklandsætta]
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in his life were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Alt. Death: 1564. 531 Skrevet: 16 Jan 2005 18:02:30 Tittel: Re: Bygdebok for Vikedal (Rogaland) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael, I am not able to find Laurits Lauritsen Opsal, f. c1611 in this document. However, Lars Knutsen Hogganvik, f. c1564 and d. 1625 is mentioned there on page 9 in the following chapter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cheers Vidar 
2 CONT
2 CONT • Occupation: Lensmann, 1591-1625, Vikedal, Ulvik, Norway. 532 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauritz married Nn Torgilsdtr on an unknown date in Norway. Nn was born on an unknown date and died on an unknown date in Hogganvik, Vikedal, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2988       i.  Lars Larsson Opsal (born on an unknown date in I Vikedal, Norway - died on an unknown date in Norway) 
2 CONT
2 CONT          ii.  Marit Larsdotter Hogganvik was born in 1570 in Hogganvik, Vikedal, Norway 520 and died on an unknown date. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lauritz next married Katrine Johannesdatter 532 in 1617.532 Another name for Katrine is Katrine Johannesdatter.531 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5977. Nn Torgilsdtr, daughter of Torgils Johannesson På Torsnes and Brigitte Sevatsdatter Skiftun, was born on an unknown date and died on an unknown date in Hogganvik, Vikedal, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nn married Lauritz Knutson Hogganvik on an unknown date in Norway. Lauritz was born in 1530 in Norway and died in 1627 in Hogganvik, Vikedal, Norway 530 aged 97. 
2 CONT
