1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Odd Sevatson Fevoll, son of Sevat Øysteinson Skiftun and Unknown, was born before 1490 in Fevoll, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway 533 and died in 1544 in Fevoll, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. Another name for Odd was 
2 CONC Odd Sjovatson Fevoll.547
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: I also have a date of death for Odd as about 1539. Auklandsætta ved Magnus Våge, Page 5, Skifte in 1621. Mentioned in 1519.
2 CONT
2 CONT Odd* SEVATSSON Fevoll was born before 1490 in Norway. He died after 1544 in Fevoll farm #53, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. He had an estate probated in 1621 in Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. Odd Sevatsson is mentioned in documents 
2 CONC in 1519, 1521, 1539 and 1544. He rented Fevold but owned half of Foss and all of Skiftun in Hjelmeland, in addition to parts of some farms in Suldal. He owned a portion of what had been the Foss estate in the Middle Ages and is li
2 CONC kely to have been descended from the family that originally owned it. In 1519, Odd paid a tax of 50 marks silver, indicating he was the largest landowner in Hjelmeland. Odd's family was involved in a long series of lawsuits with d
2 CONC istant relatives over the allodial rights to the Foss estate. According to a judgment of 31 Jul 1539, Odd was confirmed as the rightful allodial heir. Asgaut Steinnes did some research on this subject, but was not able to substant
2 CONC iate exact lines of descent. His theory, however, is that Odd's father was named Sevat Øysteinsson. He constructed a highly speculative line back through Gudrun Eilivsdatter and her husband, Eivind Sigurdsson. The earliest theoret
2 CONC ical ancestor in this line is Arne Rev. Magnus Våge mentions in "Auklandsætta" that several genealogists think Odd was descended from Odd Botolvson Finnen from Voss, a member of the Losna family. It is very possible that Odd, hims
2 CONC elf, was considered a nobleman (probably lågadel or landed gentry)
2 CONT
2 CONT Odd married Guren Thorsdatter 520 on an unknown date in Norway. Guren was born before 1500 in Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway 520 and died in 1565 in Fevoll, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway.520 Other names for Guren were Guri Toresdatte
2 CONC r,547 Guren Thorsdatter, and Guri Toresdatter.547 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.family.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~all4dad/a1.htm#i3870
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 130314. Odd* SEVATSSON Fevoll (766)(928) (777)(767) was born before 1490 in Norway. He died after 1544 in Fevoll gård #53, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. He had an estate probated in 1621 in Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. Odd Sevats
2 CONC son is mentioned in documents in 1519, 1521, 1539 and 1544. He rented Fevold but owned half of Foss and all of Skiftun in Hjelmeland, in addition to parts of some farms in Suldal. He owned a portion of what had been the Foss estat
2 CONC e in the Middle Ages and is likely to have been descended from the family that originally owned it. In 1519, Odd paid a tax of 50 marks silver, indicating he was the largest landowner in Hjelmeland. Odd's family was involved in a 
2 CONC long series of lawsuits with distant relatives over the allodial rights to the Foss estate. According to a judgment of 31 Jul 1539, Odd was confirmed as the rightful allodial heir. Asgaut Steinnes did some research on this subject
2 CONC , but was not able to substantiate exact lines of descent. His theory, however, is that Odd's father was named Sevat Øysteinsson. He constructed a highly speculative line back through Gudrun Eilivsdatter and her husband, Eivind Si
2 CONC gurdsson. The earliest theoretical ancestor in this line is Arne Rev. Magnus Våge mentions in "Auklandsætta" that several genealogists think Odd was descended from Odd Botolvson Finnen from Voss, a member of the Losna family. It i
2 CONC s very possible that Odd, himself, was considered a nobleman (probably lågadel or landed gentry).
2 CONT
2 CONT 130315. Guren* TORESDATTER (827)(767) was born about 1490 in Norway. She died in Fevoll gård #53, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 65145 i. Siri* ODDSDATTER Fevoll. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii. Sevat ODDSSON Skiftun(881) (777)(767) was born about 1510 in Fevoll gård #53, Hjelmeland, Rogaland, Norway. He died before 1570 in Sandanger, Fister, Rogaland, Norway. Sevat Oddsson appears to have first lived at Skiftun, whe
2 CONC re he operated the entire farm of 3 laupar 12 mark smør. He probably owned at least 1 laup as his daughter is credited as the owner of that amount in 1617. Sometime in the middle of the 1500's, Sevat moved to Sandanger in Fister.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 18948. Odd Savatsen (Sevatsen) FEVOLD (1187) died about 1621 in Norway. "in Hjelmeland." Mentioned 1519,21,39, 47. Administration & distribution of his estate ("skifte") in 1621. (Slooper book, p. 410a) 
2 CONT
2 CONT    "Odd Sevatsen Fevold was also ancestor of the Sloop families of Hersdal, Haukaas, Hesja, and Slogvik. He rented Fevold but he owned half of Foss and all of the Skiftun farms in Hjelmeland, parts of some farms in Suldal." (Sloop
2 CONC er book, p. 544)    
2 CONT
2 CONT    From GEDCOM file of Greg Hagen - 1996: "Odd Sevatsson is mentioned in documents in 1519, 1521, 1539 and 1544.  He rented  Fevold but owned half of Foss and all of Skiftun in Hjelmeland, in addition to parts of some farms in Sul
2 CONC dal.  He owned a portion of what had been the Foss estate in the Middle Ages and is likely to have been descended from the family that originally owned it.  In 1519, Odd paid a tax of 50 marks silver, indicating he was the largest
2 CONC  landowner in Hjelmeland.  Odd's family was involved in a long series of lawsuits with distant  relatives over the allodial rights to the Foss estate.  According to a judgment of 31 Jul 1539, Odd was confirmed as the rightful allo
2 CONC dial heir.  Asgaut Steinnes did some research on this subject, but was not able to  substantiate exact lines of descent.  His theory, however, is that Odd's father was named Sevat Øysteinsson.  He constructed a highly speculative 
2 CONC line back through Gudrun Eilivsdatter and her husband, Eivind Sigurdsson.  The earliest theoretical ancestor in this line is Arne Rev.  Magnus Vêage mentions in "Auklandsµtta" that several genealogists think Odd was descended from
2 CONC  Odd Botolvson Finnen from Voss, a member of the Losna family.  It is very possible that Odd, himself, was considered a nobleman (probably lågadel or landed gentry)." 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Guran TORESDTR..
2 CONT
2 CONT 18949. Guran TORESDTR.(1188) . Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9474 i. Savat (Sevat or Sjovat) Oddsen SKIFTUN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii. Siri Oddsdtr. FEVOLD(1189). She married Olav Jonsen Foss and was mentioned as a widow in 1563. She and Olav had a son Jon Olavsen Totland who was an ancestor of Slooper Johannes Jacobsen Steine. (Slooper book, p. 544a.) The s
2 CONC on Jon Olavsen is also an ancestor of the Slooper  Hersdal/Nelson brothers (Slooper book chart, p. 226a)  Siri and Olav also had a daughter "Magitte Olavsdatter Foss" who's line descends down to Slooper Jorgen Johnsen Hesja (Sloop
2 CONC er book chart, p. 352a) 
2 CONT
