1 NOTE {geni:about_me} P.Seland: Rafoss i Kvinesdal, s. 33-63 i Arsskrift for Agder Historielag nr 42 (1964)
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ref: Kvinesdal 2, s.393]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.nb.no/items/24f5503536691172b319fa3642d808f3?page=397
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.nb.no/items/24f5503536691172b319fa3642d808f3?page=381
2 CONT
2 CONT Død før 1568.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Aasa’s father Gase Torkelsen Rafoss, he owned six farms, hence Rafoss and Eikeland. Lagrettsmann in Mandal  LIved mostly in Rafoss Kvinsedal-His father Torkel Gunnarson Rafoss?-
2 CONT
2 CONT  Aasa died of plague before 1568.  Aase means Annie in English
2 CONT
2 CONT Her brother was Stig Gases Bagge b 1500   executed   26/10/1542 Walcheren Netherlands. Stig achieved many high ranking positions. He was knighted. In 1538 he was called ‘Stig Skau  Sten sf Vaaben”. Otherwise, he was bailiff (lord?
2 CONC ) Lista for Henrik Krummedige and since Eske Bille. He was a captain in the fleet. In 1539 he was director of mines in Norway. Stig was in the Royal Danish service in 1542. He is also known as Sean Bagge
