1 OCCU Rådmann i Bergen, Ca. 1512 Rådmann i Bergen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Tord MATSSON Losna(776) (881)(902) (926)(767) (776)(881) (902)(926) (767) was born about 1470 in Norway. He died about 1531 in Bergen, Hordaland, Norway. Tord Matsson was a businessman, alderman (rådmann) and judge in Bergen. H
2 CONC e was a "væpner", which meant that he had the right to a coat-of-arms as a member of the lower nobility. Tord was descended from the Losna family and his coat-of-arms consisted of a stack of 5 diamonds between two serpents. He is 
2 CONC mentioned in a long series of documents between 1512 and 1530. Whenever he was named together with the other rådmenn of Bergen, Tord was mentioned first. This indicates that he was the most socially prominent of the rådmenn and he
2 CONC ld the highest rank among them.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://home.online.no/~torerlan/rustung/rustung.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT # http://slektsforskning.com/login/person/anetre/tekst/Olav%20Matssoneng.asp
2 CONT # http://vagshaug.no/allslekt/1041.htm
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT # 2217
2 CONT
2 CONT Losnaætta.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vår felles slektshistorie
2 CONT
2 CONT kap 1 Losna-ætta
2 CONT
2 CONT Mats (Amundson ?) noen etterkommere
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Nevnt som rådmann i Bergen i en lang rad dokumenter fra1512 - 1530.  Når flere rådmenn nevnes, er Tord Matssøn fra 1523 - 29 alltid satt først.  I 1521 valgte Vincents Lunge "Lagmanden oc Tord Matsson" til å bære fram et sørgebu
2 CONC d til Fru Ingerd Erlendsdtr.  I 1529 var "Lagmandh och Tord Matsson och bispenn" eksekutorer i hennes bo.  I 1530 finner vi ham nevnt som avliden, men hadde etterlatt seg en sønn, Olav Tordsson.   Et brev fra 17-1-1531==regner opp
2 CONC  11  rådmenn fra Bergen, men regner ikke Tord.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Rådmann i Bergen.
