2 CONT * [https://www.nb.no/items/554e56091f23653f7f50aeca78c6897b?page=246 "Bygland gard og ætt", Bind 3 (Søndre Austad, gnr. 14, Brukarane, Torbjørn (Åsulvson) Austad, pp. 243-244)]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Is there any ''evidence'' that "Svenke Såvesen Austad", born about 1450, was married to a Guri Aasolvsdatter Sandnes, born about 1450, who was the daughter of an "Aasolv Svenkesen Sandnes", born about 1430, who was the son of a
2 CONC  "Svenke", born about 1400, who was married to a "Gitlaug Olsdtr Jondal", born about 1400, who was the daughter of "Olav Hjordal", born about 1370?'''
2 CONT The above seems to be copied from an unsubstantiated claim by Olav Harstad that [https://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang=no&pz=x&nz=anders&ocz=0&p=svenke+saveson&n=austad Svenke Såvesen Austad], born about 1450, was married to a [ht
2 CONC tps://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang=no&pz=x&nz=anders&p=gyro+aasolvsdtr&n=sandnes Gyro Aasolvsdtr Sandnes], born about 1450, who was the daughter of an [https://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang=no&pz=x&nz=anders&p=aasolv+svenkesen&n=
2 CONC sandnes Aasolv Svenkesen Sandnes], born about 1430, who was the son of a [https://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang=no&pz=x&nz=anders&p=x&n=svenke Svenke], born about 1400, who was married to a [https://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang=n
2 CONC o&pz=x&nz=anders&p=gitlaug+olsdtr&n=jordal Gitlaug Olsdtr Jordal], born about 1500 ['''note the supposed year of birth, a hundred years after her supposed husband'''], who was the daughter of [https://gw.geneanet.org/oharstad?lang
2 CONC =no&pz=x&nz=anders&p=olav+olsen&n=hjordal Olav Olsen Hjordal]  [not the supposed year of birth].
2 CONT All of these persons are listed in [https://www.nb.no/items/554e56091f23653f7f50aeca78c6897b?page=246 "Bygland gard og ætt", Bind 3, on pages 243-244]. This latter source also notes that this Åsulv Svenkesen had a daughter named G
2 CONC yro Åsulvsdatter, who again had a son named Åsulv, who again had a son named Aslak Åsulvsen, who was born about 1560. Chronologically, it seems unlikely that an "Guri Aasolvsdatter Sandnes, born about 1450" could have been the gra
2 CONC ndmother of an "Aslak Åsulvsen, born about 1560". '''It seems more likely that the Svenke Såvesen Austad, born about 1450, was married to Gitlaug Olsdtr Jondal, and that "Aasolv Svenkesen Sandnes" was their son; and thus that "Sve
2 CONC nke Såvesen Austad" and "Svenke" is one and the same person.''' Chronologically, that would make more sense. And, it is unlikely that there was many persons named Svenke in Bygland at the time, as the population of all of Bygland 
2 CONC at the time was about 280 persons, again according to [https://www.nb.no/items/554e56091f23653f7f50aeca78c6897b?page=246 "Bygland gard og ætt", Bind 3, on page 244].
