2 CONT Hertug (Duke) Knut VALDEMARSEN Denmark, born Bef. 1221 in DENMARK; died October 15, 1260;
2 CONT
2 CONT married (1) Hedvig [Patronym unkn.] av Brandenburg; married (2) Hertuginne (Dutchess) Ingegerd [Patronym
2 CONT
2 CONT unkn.] av Pommeren.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Book:
2 CONT
2 CONT Forsandboka II.58.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hertug (Duke) Knut Valdemarsen Denmark 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canute,_Duke_of_Revalia
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute or Knud Valdemarsen (died 1260) was Duke of Revelia, Blekinge and Lolland, a bastard son of King Valdemar II of Denmark. Canute was the son of the king by his concubine, Helena Guttormsdotter, widow of an important Danish n
2 CONC obleman and daughter of the late Guttorm, Riksjarl of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father gave him lands in Estonia as a hereditary duchy in 1219. He was Duke of Reval 1219-23, but was dispossessed. As compensation, he was given Blekinge in 1242, which he held until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute supported the younger rebel brothers, Abel and Christopher, against King Eric IV of Denmark in 1247. The king forced him to exchange Blekinge temporarily for Lolland, but Blekinge was soon restored to Canute's possession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Canute's wife was presumably a Wendic lady, from the ducal House of Pomerelia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He left two sons: Eric, Duke of Halland (died 1304) and Lord Svantepolk Knudsen (died ca. 1305).
2 CONT
2 CONT His land of Blekinge, with Lister, was given to his great-grandson lord Knut Folkason in the 1330s by King Magnus VII of Norway. Lord Knut's heirs continued to claim the lordship.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Valdemarsson av Danmark (död 1260), hertig av Reval (Tallinn). Utomäktenskaplig son till Valdemar II Sejr och Guttorm jarls dotter Helena.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Valdemarsson av Danmark (död 1260), hertig av Reval (Tallinn). Utomäktenskaplig son till Valdemar II Sejr och Guttorm jarls dotter Helena.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Barn 
2 CONT
2 CONT Svantepolk Knutsson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Den här artikeln är hämtad från http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knut_Valdemarsson_av_Danmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Kategorier: Hertigar | Avlidna 1260
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Knut var hertig av Reval. 1246 deltog han i Abels och Christoffers uppror mot Erik Plogpenning.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Knut Valdemarson76, born 1211 in , Denmark; died 126077.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Valdemar II, King of Denmark and Barangaria Sanchosdotter. He married of Pomerania Hedwig  Est. 1228-125377. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Knut Valdemarsson av Danmark (född cirka 1205, död 1260), hertig av Reval (Tallinn). Utomäktenskaplig son till Valdemar Sejr och Guttorm jarls dotter Helena Guttormsdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Noteringar'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Prins i Danmark, hertig i Reval. Född 1211 i Roskilde, Danmark. Död 1260 i Reval. Illegitim son till den danske konungen och den svenske jarlen Guttorms dotter Helena, änka efter den danske stormannen Esbern Snare. Knut dog i Reva
2 CONC l (Tallin), dåvarande Danmark. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hertig av Estland, Blekinge och Lolland
2 CONT
2 CONT Äger Skarsholm 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hertig av Estland, Blekinge och Lolland 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Knud Valdemarsøn (Estridsøn) Hertug af Lolland, Blekinge og Estland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fødsel:	circa 1205 Roskilde, Danmark 
2 CONT * Dødsfald:	15. oktober 1260 (50-59) Sorø, Vestsjalland, Denmark, Sorø, Danmark 
2 CONT * Begravet i:	Sct Bents, Ringsted, Sjælland, Danmark 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Søn af Valdemar Sejr, Konge af Danmark og Helene Guttormsdatter 
2 CONT * Gift med Hedevig Svantepolksdatter, von Pomerska Gdansk 
2 CONT * Far til Cecilie Knutsdotter Skarsholm; Svantepolk Knutsson og Erik Knudsen til Skarsholm 
2 CONT * Bror til NN av Valdemar Sejr Skarholm 
2 CONT * Halvbror til Niels Valdemarsen of Halland; Valdemar den Unge, Konge af Danmark; Erik IV Plovpenning, Konge af Danmark; Sophie Valdemarsdatter af Danmark; Abel Valdemarsen, Konge af Danmark; og Kong Christoffer I Valdemarsen 
2 CONT ----
