2 CONC  Teiande, a son of Ragnvald Mørejarl, but then we do not have all the names of the kindred joints between Aalov and Hjarande We are holding ourselves to the branch Harald Fairhair and down to Helge S. Munn. Finn Wang also writes, 
2 CONC "Hjardande was a Birkebeineran chieftain in the Battle of the chin cheek in 1175 and that Hjardane was very high-pitched the fact that in 1183 at the battle the egg eggs were with King Sverre's son Sigurd Lavare, sister son Håkon 
2 CONC Galen, Sverres Half-sister Peter Steyper.
