2 CONT * 2 Ingrid Ylva in legend
2 CONT * 3 Notes
2 CONT * 4 References and litterature
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Olaus Petri, she was the daughter of Sune Sik. She was married to Magnus Minnesköld of Bjelbo, possibly as his second wife. Several of his sons, born or raised by Ingrid Ylva, would come to hold positions of power whe
2 CONC n grown: Eskil became lawspeaker in Westrogothia, Karl and Bengt both became bishops of Linköping and Birger became Jarl of Sweden, and later had his son elected king.
2 CONT
