1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Princess Margrethe Haraldsdatter Gille=
2 CONT
2 CONT * MARGRETE Haraldsdatter.  Snorre names "Harald Gille's third daughter…Margaret who was married to Jon Halkelson, a brother of Simon"[474].  m ([1155]) JON Halkelsson, son of HALKEL Huk & his wife Sigrid Asulfsdatter of Rein. - ht
2 CONC tp://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''JON Halkelsson,''' son of HALKEL Huk & his wife Sigrid Asulfsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#JonHalkelssonMMargareta Project MedLands Norway]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''JON Halkelsson''' .  m  '''MARGARETA Haraldsdatter,''' illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress ---.  Snorre names "Harald Gille's third daughter…Margaret who was married to Jon Halkelson, a broth
2 CONC er of Simon". 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jon & his wife MARGARETA had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a)     '''HALLKEL Jonsson''' (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194).  From Blindheim Jarl in Norway.  m (after 19 Jun 1179) as her second husband, RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter, widow of JON Thorbergsson, daughter of ERLI
2 CONC NG Ormsen Skakke & his wife Kristin of Norway .  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[234]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Hallkel & his wife RAGNHILD had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1)       '''RAGNVALD Hallkelsson''' (-murdered Husvik near Drøbak 1217, bur Oslo).  Stormann of the Bagler in Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.tore-nygaard.com/middelalder/426.htm
2 CONT * https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Haraldsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret Haraldsdatter, Wikipedia - https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Haraldsdatter
2 CONT * Harald Gille, Wikipedia - https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harald_Gille
2 CONT * The nickname "Gille" (Gillekrist) comes from the servant Of Irish Gilla Christ.
2 CONT * In the case of Biadoc Or Bjaðok , the sources disagree. In Gaelic tradition, she is a Grandman's daughter from the Sudra Islands, which Probablymakes Harald's allegations of his own high birth. In Norwegian tradition, she is per
2 CONC ceived as a mistress. Ref.: Knut Peter Lyche Arstad. "Harald 4 Gille". In: Norwegian biographical Lexicon; 2. Utg. Bd 4. 2002
2 CONT *  A significant anecdote from the saga Of Magnussons, chap. 27, tells how Magnus pushed Harald to three times to race with a horse; Harald won all three races.
2 CONT *  Magnus Blindes and Harald Gilles saga, chap. 1
2 CONT * "The ruling water circuit...", quote from Knut Helle. Aschehoug's history of Norway. Bd 3. Under the church and royal power. 1995. S 15f
