1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Arne (Kongsmåg) Ivarsson Stodrheim==
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Son of Ivar Sunesson
2 CONT * Arne king's relation was lenderman with seat on Ståreim in Nordfjord .He was the Swedish king's daughter Ingerid Ragnvaldsdotter's fourth husband. She had previously been married to Henrik Skadelår (died 1134 ), King Harald Gill
2 CONC e (died 1136 ) and Ottar Birting (died about 1146 ), and was the mother of, among others, the Swedish heir to the throne Magnus Henriksson, King Inge Krokrygg and Orm Ivarsson Kongsbror . Arne and Ingerid had at least two children
2 CONC , Nikolas Arnesson (born about 1150 , bishop of Oslo 1190 - 1225 ) and Margrete Arnesdotter . Bagler King Philip Simonsson was their grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  ''''Queen Of Norway Ingrid Ragnvaldsdatter of Norway,''' Snorre records that Queen Ingerid married "Ottar Birting…a lendermen and a great chief, and of a Trondheim family" after the death of King Harald, but that he wa
2 CONC s killed "north in the merchant town"[455].  Snorre records that "Queen Ingerid had a son to Ivar Sneis…called Orm [surnamed]…King-brother", and afterwards married "Arne of Stodreim, who was from this called King's-mate", their ch
2 CONC ildren being "Inge, Nikolas, Philip of Herdla, and Margaret who first married Bjorn Buk and afterwards Simon Karason"
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicholas_Arnesson Nicholas Arnesson],''' Nicholas was the son of Ingrid Ragnvaldsdotter, the dowager queen of Norway and her fourth husband Arne Ivarsson of Stårheim (Árni Ívarsson). Nicholas 
2 CONC was a half-brother of King Inge I of Norway. Nicholas supported King Magnus V of Norway in the civil war against King Sverre. He fought on Magnus' side in the Battle of Ilevollene during 1180, just outside Nidaros, and appeared th
2 CONC e following year as his spokesman in negotiations with King Sverre. The conflict ended with Magnus' death in 1184 and Sverre as sole king of Norway.
2 CONT * '''[https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Arne_Kongsm%C3%A5g Margrete Arnesdotter]''' Daughter of Arne Stovreim and Queen Of Norway Ingrid Ragnvaldsdatter of Norway - (det som sto her før er slettet siden det gjaldt en helt annen Ma
2 CONC rgareta)  Married: 1st gong with Bjørn Bukk , nephew of Erling Skakke , Etne. Bjørn Bukk fell in 1179, the battle of Kalvskinnet near Nidaros .Margretha was engaged to the cowling and bellows chief ' Simon Kåreson , son of Kåre fr
2 CONC om Orre on Jæren (Olru-Kåre). According to a Danish source, he was a very rich and noble man. Orre is next door to Reve on Jæren. With Simon Kåreson,
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.nrk.no/sf/leksikon/index.php/Arne_p%C3%A5_Stodrheim Arne Stodrheim]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arne at Stodrheim as the artist Inge Rotevatn has portrayed him. Arne at Stodrheim (born approx. 1100– d. E. 1162) from Stårheim. Lendmann with large estate. He is also said to have been nicknamed Arne Kongsmåg - because he was su
2 CONC pposed to be the godfather and closest adviser to the child king Magnus Erlingson.  Magnus Erlingson.  Arne was married to Queen Ingerid Ragnvaldsdotter shortly after her third husband, lieutenant Ottar Birting, was assassinated i
2 CONC n 1147. Ingerid received the Norwegian queen title in her second marriage when she was married to King Harald Gille. Arne at Stodrheim and Queen Ingerid had four children together: the sons Inge, the "baglar bishop" Nikolas Arness
2 CONC on and Filippus at Herdla, and the daughter Margrete Arnesdotter. The son Filippus fell in the battle against King Sverre Sigurdsson at Ilevollen in Trondheim in 1180. Dotterson was earl Daughter Margrete was the mother of Filippu
2 CONC s Simonsson, an earl like his uncle, Bishop Nikolas Arnesson, with support from the Danish king Valdemar, made a failed attempt to to "King of Baglars" in 1204. In 1207, Bishop Nicholas closed with having his nephew Philip elected
2 CONC  king of the Baglar herd. - Read more about the mighty Stårheim family after lieutenant Arne at Stodrheim in the biographies of Queen Ingerid Ragnvaldsdotter, Nikolas Arnesson, Margrete Arnesdotter and Filippus Simonsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Illustreret Norges historie: bd. Fra kristendommens indførelse til Magnus, By Ole Andreas Øverland - https://books.google.com/books?id=338tAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA418&lpg=PA418&dq=Arne+at+Stodrheim+(in+Nordfjord)&source=bl&ots=z9u8bWx4fi&
