1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =BENGT Folkason "Snivel"=
2 CONT
2 CONT Tillnamnet '''snivil''' kan enligt Lagerqvist och Åberg tolkas antingen som ''den lille'' eller som ''näsvis bängel'' eller ''ha syftat på snor''. (https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bengt_snivil)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Folke The Thick, Earl of Östergötland (Folkunga) and Princess Ingegerd Knutsdotter, of Denmark 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDISH%20NOBILITY.htm#BirgerBrosadied1202 Project MedLands, Sweden Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BENGT Folkason "Snivel", son of FOLKE "den digre/the Fat" Jarl in Sweden & his wife Ingegerd of Denmark''' (-bur [Varnhem Abbey]).  Saxo Grammaticus names Ingegerd's sons Knud and Bengt[9].  '''Jarl in Sweden.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Bengt & his wife had three children:=
2 CONT
