2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mieszko_III_the_Old
2 CONT
2 CONT =Mieszko III the Old=
2 CONT '''Mieszko III the Old''' (Polish: '''Mieszko III Stary''') (ca. 1126/27 – 13 March 1202), of the Piast Dynasty, was Duke of Greater Poland, 1138–1202, and High (Senior) Duke of Poland, with interruptions, 1173–1202.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the fourth but second surviving son of '''Bolesław III Wrymouth, Duke of Poland''', by his second wife '''Salomea''', daughter of Henry, Count of Berg.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Marriages and Issue
2 CONT *Around 1136, Mieszko married firstly with '''Elisabeth''' (b. ca. 1128 - d. ca. 1154), daughter of King Béla II of Hungary.[1] They had five children:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Odon (b. ca. 1149 - d. 20 April 1194).
2 CONT # Stephen (b. ca. 1150 - d. 18 October 1166/77?).
2 CONT # Elisabeth (b. 1152 - d. 2 April 1209), married firstly ca. 1173 to Soběslav II, Duke of Bohemia and secondly aft. January 1180 to Conrad II of Landsberg, Margrave of Lusatia.
2 CONT # Wierzchoslawa Ludmilla (b. bef. 1153 - d. bef. 1223), married ca. 1167 to Frederick, Lord of Bitsch and later Duke of Lorraine.
2 CONT # Judith (b. bef. 1154 - d. af. 12 December 1201), married ca. 1173 with Bernhard, Count of Anhalt and later Duke of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT *By 1154, Mieszko married secondly with '''Eudoxia''' (b. ca. 1131 - d. aft. 1187), daughter of Grand Prince Izjaslav II of Kiev.[3] They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Bolesław (b. 1159 - killed in the Battle of Mozgawą, 13 September 1195).
2 CONT # Mieszko the Younger (b. ca. 1160/65 - d. 2 August 1193).
2 CONT # Władysław III Spindleshanks (b. ca. 1161/67 - d. 3 November 1231).
2 CONT # Salomea (b. ca. 1162/64 – d. 11 May ca. 1183), married bef. 1177 to Prince Ratibor (II) of Pomerania.
2 CONT # Anastasia (b. ca. 1164 – d. aft. 31 May 1240), married on 26 April 1177 to Bogislaw I, Duke of Pomerania.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince. Mieszko III "the Old". Born ca. 1126 Krakow, Poland. Died 13th March 1202 Kalitsz. 1st. marriage 1136/ 1140 , Erzsebet / Elisabeth Princess of Hungary Árpád(házi). 2nd marriage ca. 1151/ 1154, Jevdokia of Kiev. (informatio
2 CONC ns from genealogy Galitzine). Prince of Crakow (1173-77). Prince of Great Poland. Duke of Pomerania. 
