1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Queen Ulvhild Haakonsdotter, of Aalborg=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Håkon Finnson av Tjøtta and Brigid Ulfsdatter 
2 CONT * Ulvhild Håkonsdatter (born about 1095, died 1148) was the queen of Sweden in the 12th century , who was strongly involved in Nordic great power politics, among other things it was claimed that she was a poison killer and a stron
2 CONC g-willed intriguer.
2 CONT * Ulfhild was the queen of Sweden and Denmark, reign 1117–1125, at the same time with Ingegerd Haraldsdotter until 1118
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulvhild was married three times, with three different kings: Her first two marriages were childless. After King Nil's death, Ulvhild left Denmark for Sweden (some sources indicate that she made herself impossible in Denmark and le
2 CONC ft him before). She convinced the East Gothic chief Sverker that he would have greater prospects of being accepted even in Västergötland if he took her to wife, which also happened; In 1130, Sverker was celebrated as the entire Ki
2 CONC ng of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married '''(1) INGE II King of Sweden''' (-[1125]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  He succeeded as INGE II King of Sweden.  After his death, Magnus Nielsson of Denmark was chosen a
2 CONC s king of Sweden [Västergötland] in 1129[89].  married firstly RAGNHILD, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  St Ragnhild of Telje is identified in some sources as queen of
2 CONC  King Inge II[90].  married secondly as her first husband, ULVHILD Haakonsdotter, daughter of HAAKON Finsson & his wife --- (-before 1143). 
2 CONT * Married '''(2) Nils of Denmark''' married secondly (divorced) as her second husband, ULVHILD Haakonsdotter, widow of INGE II Halstensson King of Sweden, daughter of HAAKON Finsson & his wife --- (-before 1143).
2 CONT * Married '''(3)  Sverker the older''' Her second marriage is referred to by Saxo Grammaticus.  She was secretly abducted by Sverker I King of Sweden but their "connection was accepted as a marriage".
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm#SverkerIdied1156B Project MedLands Sweden]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''King Sverker I & his first [wife] had four children:'''
