1 NOTE Harald IV Gille King of Norway from 1136 to 1139 was killed at Bergen by Sigurd Slembi.  Harald's three sons were then joint rulers = Sigurd Mund, Ingi Krikrygg, and Eystein.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald IV Gille of Norway became ruler after he captured Magnus Sigurdson, and blinded him.  Harald reigned until 1136 when he was assassinated in Bergen by Sigurd Slembi, a pretender to the throne.
1 NOTE Det er mest sannsynlig Magnus Barfot som er Haralds far, men det er ikke
2 CONT bevist.
