2 CONT ==Gunhild Sigurdsdatter på Sylte==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Gunhild was a mistress to King SIGURD Haraldsson, son of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress Thora Guttormsdatter
2 CONT * Mistress (6): GUNHILD, wife of UNAS Kambar, sister of Nikolas Sultan
2 CONT * Mistress (6): GUNHILD, wife of UNAS Kambar, sister of Nikolas Sultan, daughter of --- (-after [1176]).  The Saga of King Sverre records that Bishop Hroi in the Faroe Islands had a brother named "Unas Kambari" married to "a Norse
2 CONC  wife…Gunnhild late in the reigns of the brothers Ingi, Sigurd and Eystein", naming her son "Sverri" whom she later claimed was the son of King Sigurd[484].  Her death is dated from the Saga of King Sverre recording that she told 
2 CONC her son who was his true father after he was 24 years old[485].  A clue about her parentage is provided by the Saga of King Sverre which records that "Nikolas Sultan…brother of King Sverri's mother" spoke at the funeral of King Ma
2 CONC gnus [in Jun 1184] - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Spouse ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: GUNHILD, wife of UNAS Kambar, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Possible Child of King SIGURD Haraldsson, son of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress Thora Guttormsdatter==
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''SVERRE Sigurdsson''' King Sigurd had one possible illegitimate son by Mistress (6): GUNHILD, wife of UNAS Kamba.6th Chid '''SVERRE Sigurdsson''' ([1152]-Bergen 9 Mar 1202, bur Bergen, Christ's Church).  The Saga of King Sver
2 CONC re records that Sverre was born in Norway as the son of Unas Kambar, and taken to the Faroe Islands when aged five, there being brought up as the foster-son of his paternal uncle Bishop Hroi.  The Saga records that his mother firs
2 CONC t told him that he was the son of King Sigurd Haraldsson when aged twenty-four, and that a year later he sailed for Norway to claim the throne[503].  It appears from the Saga that this claimed paternity was never challenged, altho
2 CONC ugh the claim was made more than twenty years after the death of his putative father and is recorded only as being based on the word of his mother.  Nor was Sverre recorded in the Saga as having been required to prove his paternit
2 CONC y by ordeal, which had been a frequent practice in similar situations in the Norwegian royal family.  King of the Birkebeine.  He succeeded in 1184 as SVERRE King of Norway.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''Project MedLands, Norway Kings - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm
2 CONT
