2 CONT “Earl Thorfinn made himself a great chief; he was the tallest and strongest of men, ugly, black-haired, sharp-featured, and big-nosed, and with somewhat scowling brows. He was a mighty man of strife, and greedy both of money and h
2 CONC onour; he was lucky in battle, and skilful in war, and good in onslaught;”
