2 CONT Sigurdsdon, Thorfinn the Black of Orkney, Jarl of Orkney. Earl of Caithness fr 1021-1064. Born: 1009 Acceded: 1014 Died: 1064 Notes: Earl of Caithness. Father: Hlodvirsson, Sigurd the Stout of Orkney, Earl of Orkney Mother: Daught
2 CONC er. Married BEF 1038 to Finnsdottir, Ingibiorg Earls Mother Child 1: Thorfinnson, Paul I of Orkney, Earl of Orkney Child 2: Thorfinnsson, Erlend II, Earl of Orkney. (Directory of Royal Genealogical Data, Hull, England)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorfinn den Mäktige var död år 1065. Birsay var en gång säte för för Orkneyjarlen. Kyrkan byggdes av jarlen Torfinn den Mäktige efter sin återkomst från en pilgrimsresa till Rom. Han styrde ett rike som omfattade nio jarldömen i 
2 CONC Skottland, Hebriderna, Isle of Man samt även stora delar av Irland. Efter hans död rasade väldet samman, Isle of Man och Hebriderna blev egna stater. (Nordisk Vikingaguide 1995, sid 169, Statens Historiska museum, Holmblad)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd married a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm, and their son was called Thorfin. Earl Sigurd had, besides, older sons; namely, Sumarlide, Bruse, and Einar Rangmund. (Heimskringla, Olov den Heliges saga III)
2 CONT
2 CONT På Birsay hade en av de största norska jarlarna sitt huvudsäte, nämligen den ärelystne och hänsynslöse Thorfinn den Mäktige. Enligt sagan uppehöll han sig ofta här och byggde även den kyrka som återfunnits. (Boken om vikingarna, s
2 CONC id 69, Catharina Ingelman-Sundberg)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorfinn, when a mere child, had been placed by him over Sutherland and Caithmess: In 1030, on the death of his half brother, Brusi, he annexed the Orkneys to his dominions. He is described as stout and strong, but very ugly; seve
2 CONC re, and cruel, but a very clever man. Duncan I, who reigned from AD. 1034-1040, attempted to deprive him of his earldom, but was himself defeated, amid his defeat was followed by his assassination in the smith's bothy, near Elgin,
2 CONC  at the hands of Macbeth, who succeeded him, and reigned from 1040-58. Thorfinn is said to have held a large Riki in Ireland, and to have extended his kingdom from Thinrso Shcerry to Dublin, and to have exacted tribute and assumed
2 CONC  the prerogatives of the earlier kings of Dublin. He died about 1064. His sons were at the battle of Stamford Bridge in 1066, and escaping from the slaughter, led a peaceful and inglorious existence as joint jarls in their norther
2 CONC n home. Ingebiorge, the widow of Thiorfinn, married Malcolm III, who reigned from 1058-93. -Robertson, i. 98, 127, and 161-2. (Chronicle of Man and the Sudreys, notes 1-2, fotnot 53)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.espell.se/saga/pc856b048.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Thorfinn Sigurdsson (c1009–-c1064), called Thorfinn the Mighty, was Earl of Orkney. One of four brothers (with Brusi, Sumarlidi and Einar) , sons of Earl Sigurd Hlodvirsson by his marriage to the daughter of Malcolm II of Scotland
2 CONC . He married Ingibiorg Finnsdottir, daughter of Finn Arnesson, Jarl of Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Heimskringla of Icelandic historian Snorri Sturluson, and the anonymous compiler of the Orkneyinga Saga, write that Thorfinn was the most powerful of all the earls of Orkney. He is said to have been earl for seventy-five years
2 CONC  and ruler of nine earldoms in Scotland, of the Hebrides, and of part of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Torfinn the Black, also called Torfinn the Mighty, Earl of Orkney, Earl of Caithness. He was born about 1000 and died about 1064. He became Orkenøyjarl after older brother. He was large, strong and wise according to Snorre. He was
2 CONC  also king in part of Scotland and Yorkshire in 1035. In Yorkshire his seat was at Wassington. Family squabbles with his half brothers marred the early part of his reign. Later his main rival was a man called Karl Hundisson the Sc
2 CONC ottish King (whom Ashley believes is the same as Duncan), Duncan/Hundisson invaded Thorfin's territory twice, loosing both times, resulting in Duncan's death which provided the opportunity for Thorfin to take over Duncan's realm. 
2 CONC Thus he became ruler of much of northern Scotland. Later in life, Thorfin became converted to Christianity, although no records indicate his baptism. He went on a tour to Rome, visited the Pope who forgave him all his past sins. H
2 CONC e established a church at Birsay, int he Orkneys. He was probably involved in Rollo's family's conquest of England (William of Normandy). After his death his kingdom was shared by his two sons, Erland and Paul.
2 CONT
2 CONT Torfinn ble også kalt Torfinn Mektige. Han var født ca år 1000 og døde ca 1064. Han ble Orkenøyjarl etter eldre brødre. Han var stor, sterk og stygg og en grisk og strid mann, men svært klok ifølge Snorre. Men han betegnes også so
2 CONC m den gjeveste jarl som hadde vært på øyene og den som hadde størst makt. Han var også konge i en del av Skottland og i Yorkshire i 1035. I Yorkshire hadde han sete i Wassington. Han var sannsynligvis engasjert i Rollo-ættlingenes
2 CONC  erobring av England. Han hadde flere betydningsfulle sønner, bl. a. Hugh of Maine som ble stamfar til det tyske huset Oldenburg, som de nåværende norske kongelige stammer fra.
