2 CONT MEDIEVAL LANDS
2 CONT
2 CONT OGMUND Thorbergsson .  His name is confirmed by Snorre naming his son "Skopte Ogmundson, a grandson of Thorberg"[46].  m ---.  The name of Ogmund´s wife is not known.  Ogmund & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         SKOPTI Ogmundsson of Giske (-Rome 1103).  Snorre names "Skopte Ogmundson, a grandson of Thorberg", when recording that he "dwelt at Giske in Sunmore"[47].  Snorre records that Skopte Ogmundson travelled from Norway with
2 CONC  his sons Ogmund, Fin and Thord, that Skopte died in Rome, and that his sons also died during the journey[48].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m GUDRUN, daughter of THORD Folason & his wife ---.  Snorre names "Gudrun, a daughter of Thord Folason" as the wife of "Skopte Ogmundson"[49].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Skopti & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv)       THORA Skoptisdatter.  Snorre names (in order) "Ogmund, Fin, Thord and Thora" as children of "Skopte Ogmundson" & his wife, specifying that Thora married "Asolf Skulason"[56].  In an earlier Saga, Snorre names "Thora, a d
2 CONC aughter of Skopte Ogmundson" as the wife of "Asolf of Reine"[57].  m ASULF Skulesson of Rein, son of SKULI Tostesson & his wife Gudrun Nefsteinsdatter.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ASULF Skulesson of Rein .  Snorre names "Asolf of Reine" as the son of Skule & his wife[224].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” as the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl Tostig Godwinson”[225].  m THORA Skop
2 CONC tisdotter, daughter of SKOPTI Ogmundsson of Giske & his wife ---.  Snorre names "Thora, a daughter of Skopte Ogmundson" as the wife of "Asolf of Reine"[226]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         GUTTORM Asulfsson of Rein .  Snorre names "Guthorm of Reine" as the son of "Asolf of Reine" & his wife[227].  Morkinskinna names “Ásólfr, the father of Guthormr at Rein” as the son of “Skúli, the son of Jarl Tostig Godw
2 CONC inson”[228]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         SIGRID .  m HALLKEL Huk.  Halkel & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          JON Halkelsson .  m ([1155]) MARGARETA Haraldsdatter, illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mistress ---.  Snorre names "Harald Gille's third daughter…Margaret who was married to Jon Halkelson, a
2 CONC  brother of Simon"[229].  Jon & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       HALLKEL Jonsson (-killed in battle Florevåg near Bergen 3 Apr 1194).  From Blindheim Jarl in Norway.  m (after 19 Jun 1179) as her second husband, RAGNHILD Erlingsdatter, widow of JON Thorbergsson, daughter of ERLING Orm
2 CONC sen Skakke & his wife Kristin of Norway .  The Saga of King Sverre records the marriage of "Ragnhild daughter of Earl Erling and Kristin Kings-daughter" and "Halkel son of Jon Hallkelsson"[230].  Hallkel & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1)       RAGNVALD Hallkelsson (-murdered Husvik near Drøbak 1217, bur Oslo).  Stormann of the Bagler in Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         SIMON Skalp (-killed in battle 1161).  Snorre names "Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk" when recording his marriage[231].  m ([1155]) MARIA Haraldsdatter, illegitimate daughter of HARALD "Gille" King of Norway & his mis
2 CONC tress ---.  Snorre names "Harald Gille's second daughter…Maria who was married to Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk"[232].  Simon & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       NIKOLAS .  Snorre names Nikolas as son of "Simon Skalp, a son of Halkel Huk" & his wife[233].  Snorre records that "Simon Skalp's son, the son of a daughter of King Harald Gille" was proposed as king in 1161[234].  
2 CONT
