1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Håkon Finnson av Tjøtta=
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Norwegian great man Håkon Finnsson of Thjottaätten (born about 1070, died 1162)  is mentioned as the father of Queen Ulvhild Håkansdotter in the book Fagrskinna , really significant "the book with the beautiful parchment ban
2 CONC d", also called Nóreg's royal number , is a collection of Norwegian kings sagas in two now lost leather manuscripts.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ulvhild Håkonsdatter,''' (born c. 1095, died 1148) was Queen of Sweden in the 1100s , who was heavily involved in Nordic superpower politics, among other things, she was alleged to be a poison killer and a willful intrigue ma
2 CONC ker. Ulvhild was married to: 1116 : Inge the younger (Halsteinsson) ( 1075 - 1125 ), Swedish king, 1130 : Nils of Denmark (Sveinsson) ( 1064 - 1134 ), Danish king, 1134 : Swedes the Elder ( 1100 - 1156 ), Swedish King.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#FinArnessondied1062 Project MedLands, Norway Nobility]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Chapter 3. DESCENDANTS of FIN SKJALGE=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Project MedLands Norway Nobility'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FIN Skjalge,''' son of --- . 
2 CONT '''married GUNHILD Halfdansdatter, daughter of HALFDAN Jarl & his wife Ingeborg of Norway [illegitimate daughter of HARALD I "Harfagri" King of Norway].'''  Snorre names Gunhild as the daughter of Halfdan & his wife[65].  Snorre n
2 CONC ames Gunhild, daughter of Earl Halfdan and Ingebjorg, as the mother of Harek's father[66]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fin Skjalge & his wife GUNHILD Halfdansdatter had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''EYVIND Skaldaspiller''' (-990).  Pöt.  m ---.  The name of Eyvind´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Eyvind & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>* a)         '''HAREK of Thjotta''' (-murdered 1040).  '''married  RAGNHILD Arnesdatter, daughter of ARNE Arnmodsson & his wife Thora Thorsteinsdatter.'''  Snorre names Ragnhild, daughter of "Arne Arnmodson and Thora, Thorstei
2 CONC n Galge's daughter" as the wife of Harek of Thjotta[67].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Harek of Thjotta & his wife RAGNHILD Arnesdatter had three children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* i)          '''EINAR Fluga of Thjotta'''
2 CONT >>>>>>* ii)         '''FIN Herkesson''' (-after 1028).  m ---.  The name of Fin´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fin Herkesson & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>* (a)       '''HAAKON Finsson''' m ---.  The name of Haakon´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Haakon & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>>>>>* (1)       '''ULVHILD Haakonsdatter''' (-before 1143).  Fagrskinna names “Úlfhildr dróttning, dóttir Hákonar Finnssunar Hárekssunar or Þjóttu” as mother of “Karl konungs”, adding that she had first married “Nikolás Dana
2 CONC konungr”, secondly “Ingi Sviakonungr Hallsteinssunr” and thirdly “Sverkir konungr Kolssunr”[68].  Her second marriage is referred to by Saxo Grammaticus.  She was secretly abducted by Sverker I King of Sweden but their "connection
2 CONC  was accepted as a marriage"[69].  '''married firstly as his second wife, INGE II Halstensson King of Sweden, son of HALSTEN Stenkilsson King of Sweden & his wife''' --- (-1118).  '''married secondly (divorced) as his second wife,
2 CONC  NIELS King of Denmark, illegitimate son of SVEND II King of Denmark & his mistress --- (-murdered Schleswig 25 Jun 1134).''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>>* iii)        '''SVEN Harkesson'''
2 CONT * 2.         '''NJAL Finsson''' m ---.  The name of Njal´s wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' NJAL Finsson & his wife had one child'''
2 CONT
