2 CONT
2 CONT TEXT
2 CONT
2 CONT Her older sister Bethoc married Crínán of Dunkeld, and her other sister Donada married Findláich, Mormaer of Moray. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd married one of King Malcolm's daughters. Bethoc was her sister, but her name is not known from the sagas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The saga says:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd married a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm, and their son was called Thorfin. Earl Sigurd had, besides, older sons; namely, Sumarlide, Bruse, and Einar Rangmund. Their mother was an anonymous "frille", a mistress.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Gaelic, Olith would be "Olith ingen Maíl Coluim meic Cináeda", Olith daughter of Malcolm McKenneth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some claim her name was Donada. This source states that Malcolm's daughter Olith married Sigurd, while Donada married Finlay. http://macdonnellofleinster.org/page_7y__the_birth_of_scotland.htm 
2 CONT
2 CONT Since Malcolm II, King of Scots, had no son of his own, he undertook to negotiate a series of dynastic marriages of his three daughters to men who might otherwise be his rivals, while securing the loyalty of the principal chiefs, 
2 CONC their relatives. First he married his daughter Bethoc to Crinan, Thane of The Isles, head of the house of Atholl and secular Abbot of Dunkeld; then his youngest daughter, Olith, to Sigurd, Earl of Orkney. His middle daughter, Dona
2 CONC da, was married to Findláich, Mormaer of Moray, Thane of Ross and Cromarty and a descendant of Loarn of Dalriada. This was risky business under the rules of succession of the Gael, but he thereby secured his rear and, taking advan
2 CONC tage of the renewal of Viking attacks on England, marched south to fight the Sasunnaich. He defeated the Angles at Carham in 1018 and installed his grandson, Duncan, son of the Abbot of Dunkeld and his choice as Tanist, in Carlisl
2 CONC e as King of Cumbria that same year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Saga of St Olav" by Snorri Sturlusson
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death Earl Sigurd showed no obedience or fealty to King Olaf. He married a daughter of the Scottish king Malcolm, and their son was called Thorfin. Earl Sigurd had, besides, older sons; namely, Sumarlide, Bruse, and Eina
2 CONC r Rangmund. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Four or five years after Olaf Tryggvason's fall Earl Sigurd went to Ireland, leaving his eldest sons to rule the country, and sending Thorfin to his mother's father, the Scottish king. On this expedition Earl Sigurd fell in Brian'
2 CONC s battle. When the news was received in Orkney, the brothers Sumarlide, Bruse, and Einar were chosen earls, and the country was divided into three parts among them. Thorfin Sigurdson was five years old when Earl Sigurd fell. When 
2 CONC the Scottish king heard of the earl's death he gave his relation Thorfin Caithness and Sutherland, with the title of earl, and appointed good men to rule the land for him. Earl Thorfin was ripe in all ways as soon as he was grown 
2 CONC up: he was stout and strong, but ugly; and as soon as he was a grown man it was easy to see that he was a severe and cruel but a very clever man."
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
