1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hvordan Kale Kolsson ble kalt Ragnvald''': "...kong Sigurd [Jorsalfare] ga Kale Kolsson halve Orkenøyene ved siden av Pål Håkonsson jarl. Kale fikk også jarletittel. Kong Sigurd ga ham i tillegg navnet Ragnvald 
2 CONC jarl etter Ragnvald Brusesson. For Gunnhild, mor hans, sa at Ragnvald Brusesson hadde vært den ypperste av alle jarler i Orkenøyene og syntes det ville bringe lykke for Kale. Denne delen av Orkenøyene hadde Magnus jarl, morbroren 
2 CONC til Kale, hatt." Flatøybok pkt 390 (bind IV side 95)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Saitn Rögnvaldr III "Kali" (the Holy), jarl of Orkney''' (c1100-1158), warrior chieftain in the Orkney Islands, Scotland. According to tradition, he made a vow to build a church, fulfilling the pledge by erecting the cathedral 
2 CONC of St. Magnus at Kirkwall. Ronald was later murdered by a group of rebelling warriors and was venerated as a martyr at Kirkwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Feast Day: August 20
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R%C3%B6gnvald_Kali_Kolsson
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Erlendottir/6000000001169154976 GUNHILD].  ''Orkneyinga Saga'' names “[http://www.geni.com/people/Gunhild-Erlendottir/6000000001169154976  Gunnhild] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Cecilia-Erlen
2 CONC dsdatter/6000000008177258360 Cecilia]” as the two daughters of “Earl Erlend Thorfinnson” and his wife “Thora, the daughter of Sumarlidi Ospaksson”[913].  Orkneyinga Saga records that [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-III-Olavsson
2 CONC -%C2%ABBarefoot%C2%BB-Berrf%C3%B8tt/5381202464070053447 Magnus "Barelegs"] King of Norway “gave Earl Erlend´s daughter Gunnhild in marriage to [http://www.geni.com/people/Kol-Kali-Lalisson/6000000001169130795?through=6000000001169
2 CONC 154976  Kol], son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-S%C3%A6bj%C3%B8rnson/6000000003820968938?through=6000000001169130795  Kali Sæbjarnarson], in compensation for the death of his father”, adding that her dowry was “some property
2 CONC  in Orkney including a farm at Paplay” and that the couple “settled down on his estate at Agder”[914].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>m (Spring 1099) [http://www.geni.com/people/Kol-Kali-Lalisson/6000000001169130795?through=6000000001169154976  KOL] Kalisson, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-S%C3%A6bj%C3%B8rnson/6000000003820968938?through=6000000001169
2 CONC 130795  KALI] of Agdir in Norway & his wife ---.  Lenderman in Agder.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Kol & his wife had two children:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>1. [http://www.geni.com/people/Kali-Agder/6000000003820968970?through=6000000001169130795  KALI] [Rognvald] ([1100]-murdered Force, Calder, Caithness 20 Aug 1158, bur St Magnus Cathedral).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Kali and…[http
2 CONC ://www.geni.com/people/Ingrid-Fot/6000000001169154985?through=6000000001169130795  Ingirid]” as the two children of “Kol, son of Kali Sæbjarnarson” and his wife[915].  Invested as Jarl, given the name Ragnvald and ½ Orkney in 1129
2 CONC  by Sigurd I Jorsalafari King of Norway.  The latter's successor, Magnus IV "the Blind", cancelled the gift in [1130].  Harald "Gilli" King of Norway invested him as Jarl of ½ Orkney in Spring 1135.  Jarl Paul refused to give up a
2 CONC ny territory to him.  In revenge Kali-Rognvald seized the Shetlands, but his men were defeated in Yell Sound 27 Jun 1135 by Jarl Paul.  He seized the Shetlands again in 1137, and captured and deposed Paul, becoming Jarl of all Ork
2 CONC ney and Caithness.  He granted ½ Orkney in 1139 to Harald Maddadsson.  Leaving Harald in charge of Orkney, he sailed for Palestine in 1151, returning in Dec 1155.  He was murdered by Thorbiorn Clerk.  Orkneyinga Saga records that 
2 CONC “Earl Rognvald died on the fifth day after the Feast of the Assumption” and was buried “at St Magnus´ Cathedral”[916]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>m ---.  The name of Kali-Rognvald´s wife is not known.  Kali-Rognvald & his wife had one child:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>[http://www.geni.com/people/Ingirid-R%C3%B6gnvaldsd%C3%B3ttir/6000000003820968980 INGIGERD].  Orkneyinga Saga records the marriage of “Earl Rognvald…his daughter Ingerid” and “[http://www.geni.com/people/Eric-Slagbrellir/60000
2 CONC 00003820968990?through=6000000003820968980 Eirik Stay-Brails]”[917].
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>m (Sutherland Spring 1156) [http://www.geni.com/people/Eric-Slagbrellir/6000000003820968990?through=6000000003820968980 ERIK] Slagbrellir, son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Edmund-de-VINGULMARK-de-SU%C3%88DE/60000000005717562
2 CONC 82?through=6000000003820968990 ERIL Streita] & his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Au%C3%B0hildr/6000000003828029604?through=6000000003820968990 Audhild] [daughter of Thorliot].  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>Erik & his wife had [seven] children:  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>(1)       [http://www.geni.com/people/Harald-3-The-Young-of-Orkneys/6000000003820968995?through=6000000003820968990  HARALD] Eriksson "Ungi" ([1156]-killed in battle Wick 1198).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>(2)       [http://www.geni.com/people/Magnus-Slagbrellir/6000000017406048293 MAGNUS] Mangi (-killed in battle near Fimreite on Sognefjord 15 Jun 1184).  Orkneyinga Saga names (in order) “Harald the Young, Magnus Mangi and Rog
2 CONC nvald” as the three sons of “Eirik Stay-Brails”, adding that Magnus was killed with Magnus V Erlingsson King of Norway “at Sogn”[920].  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#_Toc268450047 (Cawley's Medlands)]
