2 CONT ..'''She has now been conclusively identified'''[4][5] as the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Isaac-Komnenos-Vatatzes/6000000088516333907 Isaac Komnenos Vatatzes], <br/>
2 CONT ''the grandson of the Byzantine general [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodoros-Vatazes/6000000002188294092 Theodore Vatatzes] and the purple-born princess [https://www.geni.com/people/Eudokia-Komnene/6000000003087173515 Eudokia Ko
2 CONC mnene], daughter of Emperor [https://www.geni.com/people/John-II-the-Good-Eastern-Roman-Emperor/6000000002979868893 John II Komnenos] (r. 1118–1143),[6] ''<br/>
2 CONT and of [https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Lascarina/6000000000467542216 Anna Komnene Angelina], the second daughter of Emperor [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexios-III-byzantine-emperor/6000000000515214098 Alexios III Angelos] ).[7
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her parents married in or slightly before '''1190''', and Theodora was born shortly after, since in 1203 she was just entering her fourteenth year.[8]
2 CONT
