2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sveinke_Steinarsson Sveinke Steinarsson, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sveinke Steinarsson , or Svenke Steinarsson was a lieutenant in Norway at the end of the 1000s . He was the father of Ragnhild , who married the western chief Kyrpinge-Orm Sveinsson . Ragnhild and Kyrpinge-Orm had a son Erling Ska
2 CONC kke , known as one of the leaders of the lieutenant party and father of King Magnus Erlingsson ( Norwegian king 1161 - 1184 ).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Foster Father of a King's Son?'''	
2 CONT
2 CONT Sveinke is mentioned in Snorre 's Haraldssønnenes saga when Snorre describes Erling Skakke's family , [1] but otherwise Snorre has no information about Sveinke. In the saga Morkinskinna , however, we learn more about him. Sveinke 
2 CONC is said to have been the foster father of King Håkon Magnusson Toresfostre , who was the son of King Magnus Haraldsson and the grandson of King Harald Hardråde . According to the unknown author of Morkinskinna, Håkon was brought u
2 CONC p by Sveinke, and only later came to Tore on Steig , who is known as Håkon's foster father. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lendmann'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sveinke was a rich and powerful lieutenant who lived in Viken , in Ranrike ( Båhuslen ), just east of Gøta river . In the Middle Ages , this was part of Norway. Here he had several farms. The fact that Sveinke was Håkon's foster f
2 CONC ather must have led to a conflict with King Magnus Berrføtt . Håkon and Magnus were cousins, and after Magnus' father Olav Kyrre's death, both were proclaimed kings, Håkon in Trøndelag and Magnus in Viken. [3] Sveinke lived in Vik
2 CONC en, but since he had been Håkon's foster father, he was loyal to him, and did not want to submit to Magnus. [4] Magnus therefore sent the Trøndelag womanthe lieutenant Sigurd Ullstreng , as well as three other Vikvær lieutenants, 
2 CONC among them Dag Eilivsson , to get Sveinke to accept Magnus as his master. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sveinke would rather leave the country than submit to King Magnus, so he was gone for three winters. In Sveinke's absence, however, there was unrest in the area, and it ended up that King Magnus had to ask Sveinke to return. Svein
2 CONC ke now got his properties back, and he and Magnus entered into a friendship ( alliance ). [6]
2 CONT
