2 CONT * Son of Kong Stenkil Ragnvaldsson av Sverige and Queen Ingamoder 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (1) '''HELENA,''' Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 1194/95 which names “Cristinæ Reginæ…filia…Ingonis Suevorum Regis et Helena Reginæ”[95].  Presumably Helena originated in Russia where her husband allegedly 
2 CONC lived before 1080.  She is first named in Abbot William's genealogy of the Danish kings written in [1193][96].  Her possible Russian or Byzantine origin, and whether the series of Greek names were introduced into the Swedish royal
2 CONC  family through her influence, is discussed by M. Sjöström
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married (2) ''' MAER,''' She is the wife attributed to King Inge in the Sagas, but as "Maer" means "the maiden" she may be identical with his first wife shown above[120].  However, Sjöström suggests that Queen Helena´s religious
2 CONC  donations indicate that this is unlikely to be correct because Blot-Sven is recorded in primary sources as a heathen[121].  m as his second wife, INGE I Stenkilson King of Sweden, son of STENKIL Ragnvaldsson King of Sweden & his 
2 CONC wife --- Emundsdottir (-[1111])
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWEDEN.htm '''Project MedLands- Sweden''']
2 CONT
2 CONT INGE Stenkilsson (-[1111]).  Snorre names Inge as son of Stenkel when recording that he succeeded Hakon as king[93].  He lived in Russia before being recalled to Sweden to become king, although the primary source on which this sta
2 CONC tement is based has not yet been identified.  He succeeded in 1080 as INGE I King of Sweden.  Orkneyinga Saga records that “King Ingi Steinkelsson” was deposed because of his Christianity and replaced by “another king who still ad
2 CONC hered to the pagan rites, the queen´s brother Svein, nicknamed the Sacrificer”, adding that Inge “was forced into exile and went to West Gotaland, but eventually managed to trap Svein inside a house and burnt him there” before res
2 CONC uming control[94].  '''married firstly HELENA,''' daughter of ---.  Her marriage is confirmed by a charter dated 1194/95 which names “Cristinæ Reginæ…filia…Ingonis Suevorum Regis et Helena Reginæ”[95].  Presumably Helena originate
2 CONC d in Russia where her husband allegedly lived before 1080.  She is first named in Abbot William's genealogy of the Danish kings written in [1193][96].  Her possible Russian or Byzantine origin, and whether the series of Greek name
2 CONC s were introduced into the Swedish royal family through her influence, is discussed by M. Sjöström[97].  '''married secondly MAER, sister of BLOT-SVEN [later King of Sweden].'''  She is the wife attributed to King Inge in the Saga
2 CONC s, but as "Maer" means "the maiden" she may be identical with his first wife shown above[98].  However, Sjöström suggests that Queen Helena´s religious donations indicate that this is unlikely to be correct because Blot-Sven is re
2 CONC corded in primary sources as a heathen[99]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =King Inge & his first wife Helena had four children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''CHRISTINA''' (-18 Jan 1122).  Fagrskinna records that “Harald konungr”, son of “Valdimars ok Gydu”, married “Kristinar, dóttur Inga konungs Steinkelssunar”[100].  Morkinskinna records that “Haraldr Valdimarsson” ma
2 CONC rried “Kristin, the daughter of King Ingi Steinkelsson king of the Swedes”[101].  A genealogy written by Vilhelm Abbot of Æbelholt records that “Christina avia Waldemari regis filia fuit Ingonis Svevorum regis et Helene regine”[10
2 CONC 2].  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a charter dated 1194/95 which names “Ingiburgh filia Rizlavi…Ruthenorum Regis et Cristinæ Reginæ…filia…Ingonis Suevorum Regis et Helena Reginæ”[103].  m (1095) as his first wife, MS
2 CONC TISLAV I Vladimirovich Grand Prince of Kiev, son of VLADIMIR Vsevolodich "Monomakh" Grand Prince of Kiev & his first wife Gytha of England (1076-15 Apr 1132). 
2 CONT * b)         '''MARGRETA "Fredkulla/peace-bringing woman''' (-4 Nov [1130], bur Roskilde).  Snorre records that the marriage of "King Inge's daughter Margaret" and King Magnus was agreed at "Konghelle on the Gaut river" under the 
2 CONC agreement which settled disputes between the kings of Norway, Denmark and Sweden[104].  Saxo records that her first marriage took place after the peace meeting between the three Scandinavian kings at Gotaalv in 1101, hence her nic
2 CONC kname[105].  Snorre names "Queen Margaret, a daughter of King Inge, who had before been married to King Magnus Barefoot" as the wife of "the Danish king Nikolas, a son of Svein Ulfson"[106].  m firstly ([1101]) MAGNUS III "Berrføt
2 CONC t/Barfod/Barfot/Barefoot" King of Norway, illegitimate son of OLAV III "Kyrre/the Gentle" King of Norway & his mistress --- (-killed in battle in Ireland 24 May 1103).  m secondly ([1105]) as his first wife, NIELS King of Denmark,
2 CONC  illegitimate son of SVEND II King of Denmark & his mistress --- (-murdered Schleswig 25 Jun 1134).
2 CONT * c)        ''' KATARINA,''' The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not so far been identified.  m BJØRN "Jernside/Ironside" of Denmark, son of HARALD "Kesja" Regent of Denmark & his wife Ragnhild of Norw
2 CONC ay (-drowned 1134).
2 CONT * d)        ''' RAGVALD Ingesson'''  His parentage is given in the Fagrskinna genealogy[107].  Snorre names "Ragnvald, who was the son of the Swedish King Inge Steinkelson" when recording his daughter's marriage[108].  Claimant to
2 CONC  the throne.  Under-King in Västergötland.  He was killed when he arrived uninvited at the ting at Karlaby[109].  m ---.  The name of Ragvald's wife is not known.  Ragvald & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT >>>>>* i)          INGRID Ragvaldsdotter
