2 CONC "[1136].  m SOPHIE, daughter of --- (-26 Jun [1110], bur ---, transferred to Zwiefalten).  Ortlieb's Chronicon of Zwiefalten names "Bobbonis comitis et Sophiæ ipsius uxori", when recording that their son Heinrich transferred their
2 CONC  remains to Zwiefalten[1137].  The necrology of Zwiefalten records the death "VI Kal Jul" of "Sophia com de Berge"[1138].  Europäische Stammtafeln[1139] shows Sophia, wife of Graf Poppo, as Sophia of Hungary, daughter of Salomon K
2 CONC ing of Hungary.  
