2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yaropolk_Izyaslavich
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Yaropolk Pjotr Izyaslavich==
2 CONT Yaropolk Izyaslavich[2] (died 1087) was a Knyaz (prince) during the eleventh-century in the Kievan Rus' kingdom and was the King of Rus (1076–1078). The son of Grand Prince Izyaslav Yaroslavich by a Polish princess named Gertruda,
2 CONC  he is visible in papal sources by the early 1070s but largely absent in contemporary Rus sources until his father's death in 1078. During his father's exile in the 1070s, Yaropolk can be found acting on his father's behalf in an 
2 CONC attempt to gain the favor of the German emperors and the papal court of Pope Gregory VII. His father returned to Kiev in 1077 and Yaropolk followed.
2 CONT ===Family background===
2 CONT Yaropolk was the son of Izyaslav Yaroslavich (died 1078), over-king of the Rus', and Gertruda, daughter of the Polish Duke-King Mieszko II Lambert (died 1034).[4] Since the Kievan succession war of 1015-1019, the Polish ruler Bole
2 CONC slaw had taken an interest in Rus, hoping to gain control of the land of Cherven, seized by Vladimir the Great.[5]
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT * Wife - Kunigunde, daughter of Otto
2 CONT ** 1.Anastasia (daughter), married Gleb Vseslavich
2 CONT ** 2. ? (daughter), married Günther, Count of Schwarzburg
2 CONT ** 3.Yaroslav (son) (?-1102)
2 CONT ** 4.Viacheslav (son) (?-1104)
2 CONT ** 5.Vasilko (son)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was installed as Prince of Volynia and, maybe, Turov by his uncle Vsevolod Grand Prince of Kiev in 1078, but was expelled in 1085 by his cousin Vladimir "Monomakh" and found refuge in Poland.  He was restored the following year
2 CONC  but murdered soon after.
