1 NOTE Tords ætt og hjem kjennes ikke. Hans hustru, Ålov, var imidlertid datter til Einar Tambarskjelve og Bergliot, datter til Håkon Jarl. Han må derfor selv også ha vært "ættestor".
2 CONT
2 CONT Han var en av dem som i 1018 oppdaget Røreks mordplan mot Olav. Under slaget ved Stiklestad var han kong Olav den Helliges merkesmann og gikk i spissen med kongens merke høyt på den fagre gyldne stand. Han falt under merket.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Olaf Haraldson the Saint's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "224. OF THORD FOLASON.
2 CONT Thord Folason carried King Olaf's banner. So says Sigvat the skald, in the death-song which he composed about King Olaf, and put together according to resurrection saga: --
2 CONT "Thord. I have heard, by Olaf's side,
2 CONT Where raged the battle's wildest tide,
2 CONT Moved on, and, as by one accord
2 CONT Moved with them every heart and sword.
2 CONT The banner of the king on high,
2 CONT Floating all splendid in the sky
2 CONT From golden shaft, aloft he bore, --
2 CONT The Norsemen's rallying-point of yore." "
2 CONT
2 CONT "238. BEGINNING OF THE BATTLE OF STIKLESTAD.
2 CONT ... Then the bonde-army pushed on from all quarters. They who stood in front hewed down with their swords; they who stood next thrust with their spears; and they who stood hindmost shot arrows, cast spears, or threw stones, hand-a
2 CONC xes, or sharp stakes. Soon there was a great fall of men in the battle. Many were down on both sides. In the first onset fell Arnljot Gelline, Gauka-Thorer, and Afrafaste, with all their men, after each had killed a man or two, an
2 CONC d some indeed more. Now the ranks in front of the king's banner began to be thinned, and the king ordered Thord to carry the banner forward, and the king himself followed it with the troop he had chosen to stand nearest to him in 
2 CONC battle; and these were the best armed men in the field, and the most expert in the use of their weapons. ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "239. THORGEIR OF KVISTSTAD'S FALL.
2 CONT King Olaf fought most desperately. He struck Thorgeir of Kviststad across the face, the lenderman before mentioned, cut off the nose-piece of his helmet, and clove his head down below the eyes so that they almost fell out. When he
2 CONC  fell the king said, "Was it not true, Thorgeir, what I told thee, that thou shouldst not be victor in our meeting?" At the same instant Thord stuck the banner-pole so fast in the earth that it remained standing. Thord had got his
2 CONC  death-wound, and fell beneath the banner.
2 CONT There also fell Thorfin Mun, and also Gissur Gullbrarskald, who was attacked by two men, of whom he killed one, but only wounded the other before he fell. ..."
1 NOTE He was King Olav den Helliges's Standard Bearer.
1 NOTE Tord Foleson er kjent fra Slaget på Stiklestad der han var Olav Haraldsson (Senere Olav den hellige)s merkesmann. Han gikk i spissen med kongens merke høyt på den fagre gyldne stand. Han falt under merket 29. juli 1030.
2 CONT
2 CONT Historien om Tord Foleson har inspirert dikteren Per Sivle til diktet: ?Tord Foleson?. Siste vers fra dette diktet, her i versjon 1901, blir ofte resitert:
2 CONT
2 CONT ?Mannen kan siga, 
2 CONT men Merket det maa 
2 CONT i Noreg si Jord 
2 CONT som paa Stiklestad staa. 
2 CONT Og det er det stora, 
2 CONT og det er det glupa, 
2 CONT at Merket det stend, 
2 CONT um Mannen han stupa.? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Diktet blir tatt til inntekt for heltedåd og selvoppofrelse i strid, noe som har inspirert mange. Et eksempel er at verset fantes på NS-monumentet på Stiklestad
