1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Gertrud of Saxony (Schweinfurt around 1030 - Veurne 4 Aug 1113, bur Veurne)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Bernard (after 990-29 Jun 1059, bur Lüneburg St Michael) m [1020]) Eilika von Schweinfurt
2 CONT
2 CONT x ([1050]) Floris I Count of Holland
2 CONT >>1.         Dirk  ([1050/55]-17 Jun 1091, bur Egmond).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>2.         Floris (-before 1061, bur Egmond).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>3.         Peter?  Canon at St Lambert in Liège.  He is named in Europäische Stammtafeln[360], but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.  No record of another individual named Peter has been foun
2 CONC d in this family, which suggests that his identification as a son of Count Dirk IV should be viewed with scepticism. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>4.         Bertha of Holland ([1058]-Montreuil-sur-Mer, Pas-de-Calais 15 Oct 1094).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>5.         Adela [Christina] (-1085).  
2 CONT
2 CONT xx (1063) Robert de Flandre
2 CONT >>6.         Adela de Flandre ([1065]-Apr 1115).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>7.         Robert (1065-[5 Oct] 1111, bur Arras St Vaast).
2 CONT
2 CONT >>8.         Phillipe de Flandres "de Loo" (-before 1127).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>9.         Ogive? de Flandre (before 1071-Apr before 1141).  
2 CONT
2 CONT >>10.         Baudoin? de Flandre (-before 1080).  He is named as son of Count Robert in Europäische Stammtafeln[375] but the primary source on which this is based has not yet been identified.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>11.         Gertrude de Flandre (-[1115/26]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[https://geneall.net/en/name/2094/gertrudis-of-saxe/ Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#Gertruddied1113 Medlands]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT BERNHARD (after 990-29 Jun 1059, bur Lüneburg St Michael).   m ([1020]) EILIKA von Schweinfurt, daughter of HEINRICH von Schweinfurt Markgraf der Nordgau & his wife Gerberga [von Hammerstein] ([1000]-10 Dec after [1055/56]).   Duk
2 CONC e Bernhard II & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >c)         '''GERTRUD of Saxony''' (Schweinfurt [1028]-Veurne 4 Aug 1113, bur Veurne).  The Genealogica Comitum Flandriæ Bertiniana names "filiam Bernardi Saxonum comitis Gertrudem" as wife of "Robertus", specifying that she was 
2 CONC "viduam Florentii comitis Fresonum"[341].  The Chronologia Johannes de Beke records the marriage of Count Floris and "Gertrudim filiam Hermanni ducis Saxonum"[342], "Hermanni" being an error for "Bernardi" as the former would be i
2 CONC mpossible chronologically.  "Gertrudis" is named as wife of "Roberti Frisonis" in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin, which does not give her origin[343].  The Genealogia ex stirpe Sancti Arnulfi names "Idam Namucensem…uxorem Angelber
2 CONC ti marchionis et Gertrudem comitissam Flandrensem" as children of "Bernardum"[344].  The Annales Egmundani specify that Robert acquired the "comitatum Hollandiæ et Fresiæ" by marrying Gertrud[345].  [The necrology of the abbey of 
2 CONC Saint-Denis records the death "XV Kal Aug" of "Gertrudis comitissa"[346].  It is uncertain whether this entry relates to the widow of Count Floris and Count Robert.]  Beke's Egmondsch Necrologium records the death "IV die Aug" of 
2 CONC "Gheertrudis…" and her burial in Flanders[347].  [A manuscript catalogue of benefactors to Eversham monastery records the death “1 aprilis” 1113 of “Robertus Hierosolymitanus...Gertrudis mater eius”[348].  The accuracy of this sou
2 CONC rce is unknown.  The latest date recorded is 1629, but it is not known whether the document represents a later compilation based on earlier sources.]  m firstly ([1050]) FLORIS I Count of Holland, son of DIRK III Count of Holland 
