2 CONT >>d)         BERTHA of Holland ([1058]-Montreuil-sur-Mer, Pas-de-Calais 15 Oct 1094).  The Liber Modernorum Regum Francorum records the marriage of "filiam ducis Frisiæ" and "rex Philippus"[361].  The Chronologia Johannes de Beke 
2 CONC names (in order) "Theodricum et Florencium…et Machtildim" as children of Count Floris & his wife, specifying that "Machtildim" married "Philippus rex Francie" after the death of her father which indicates that "Machtildim" in this
2 CONC  text is an error for Bertha[362].  The Historia Francorum names "filiam Florentii ducis Frisonum Bertam" as wife of King Philippe[363].  Her marriage was arranged as part of the settlement under which her future husband recognise
2 CONC d her stepfather as Count of Flanders[364].  Her husband sent her to Montreuil after repudiating her.  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Victor records the death "Id Oct" of "Berta mater Ludovici regis"[365].  Clarius’s Chronico
2 CONC n Sancti Petri Vivi Senonensis records the death in 1094 of “Berta regina, quæ a rege Philippo prius fuerat derelicta”[366].  m (1072, repudiated 1092) as his first wife, PHILIPPE I King of France, son of HENRI I King of France & 
2 CONC his second wife Anna Iaroslavna of Kiev (1052-château de Melun, Seine-et-Marne 30 Jul 1108, bur Abbaye Saint Benoît-sur-Loire).http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HOLLAND.htm#FlorisIdied1061
