2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Spytihn%C4%9Bv-II-duke-of-Bohemia/6000000002176664000 Spytihněv II] '''Successor:''' Him self as King  Title next held by [https://www.geni.com/people/Conrad-I-duke-of-Bohemia/60000
2 CONC 00006906570375 Conrad I]
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''King of Bohemia:''' reign 1085–1092
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' New title '''Successor:''' Vacant Title next held by [https://www.geni.com/people/Vladislav-II-King-of-Bohemia/6000000001477171801 Vladislaus II] from 1158.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vratislaus II or Wratislaus II (Czech: Vratislav II) (died 14 January 1092), the son of Bretislaus I and Judith of Schweinfurt, daughter of Henry of Schweinfurt, was the first King of Bohemia from 15 June 1085. The royal title was
2 CONC  a grant, however, from the Holy Roman Emperor and was not hereditary. Before being raised to kingship, he had ruled Bohemia as duke since 1061. He was one of the greatest of medieval Bohemian rulers.
2 CONT
