1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Grand Prince Vladimir had nine illegitimate children by unknown Mistresses (3) to (9): 
2 CONT 16.       '''DOBRONEGA MARIA Vladimirovna (before 1012-1087).  The Primary Chronicle records the marriage of "Yaroslav's sister" to Kazimierz of Poland in 1043 but does not name her[145].  The Annales Polanorum state that "Kazimir
2 CONC um duxit ex Russia Mariam" in 1025[146], although the date is clearly inaccurate.  The Chronicæ Polanorum refers to the wife of King Kazimierz as "de Rusia nobilem"[147].  The Chronica principum Polonie records that "Kazimirus" ma
2 CONC rried "Dobrognewam"[148].  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record the death in 1087 of "Dobronega uxor Kazimir"[149].  m (1043) KAZIMIERZ I KAROL "Odnowiciel/the Renewer" Prince of Poland, son of MIESZKO II Lambert King of Polan
2 CONC d & his wife Richeza [Ezzonen] (25 Jul 1016-19 Mar 1058).''' 
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Dobroniega_of_Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I26030&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift 1041 med 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kasimir I Karol av Polen, född 1016, död 1058. furste. restaurator.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT  DOBRONEGA MARIA Vladimirovna (before 1012-1087).  The Primary Chronicle records the marriage of "Yaroslav's sister" to Kazimierz of Poland in 1043 but does not name her[135].  The Annales Polanorum state that "Kazimirum duxit ex 
2 CONC Russia Mariam" in 1025[136], although the date is clearly inaccurate.  The Chronicæ Polanorum refers to the wife of King Kazimierz as "de Rusia nobilem"[137].  The Chronica principum Polonie records that "Kazimirus" married "Dobro
2 CONC gnewam"[138].  The Annales Capituli Cracoviensis record the death in 1087 of "Dobronega uxor Kazimir"[139].  m (1043) KAZIMIERZ I KAROL "Odnowiciel/the Renewer" Prince of Poland, son of MIESZKO II Lambert King of Poland & his wife
2 CONC  Richeza [Ezzonen] (25 Jul 1016-19 Mar 1058).  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Family life and children of Vladimir I
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT German wife of Vladimir I
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Porphyrogeneta is known to have predeceased Vladimir by four years. Thietmar of Merseburg, writing from contemporary accounts, mentions that Boleslaw I of Poland captured Vladimir's widow during his raid on Kiev in 1018. The 
2 CONC historians long had no clue as to identity of this wife. The emigre historian Nicholas Baumgarten, however, pointed to the controversial record of the "Genealogia Welforum" and the "Historia Welforum Weingartensis" that one daught
2 CONC er of Count Kuno von Oenningen (future Duke Konrad of Swabia) by "filia Ottonis Magni imperatoris" (Otto the Great's daughter; possibly Rechlinda Otona [Regelindis], claimed by some as illegitimate daughter and by others legitimat
2 CONC e, born from his first marriage with Edith of Wessex) married "rex Rugorum" (king of Russia). He interpreted this evidence as pertaining to Vladimir's last wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is believed that the only child of this alliance was Dobronega, or Maria, who married Casimir I of Poland between 1038 and 1042. As her father Vladimir died about 25 years before that marriage and she was still young enough to 
2 CONC bear at least five children, including two future Polish dukes (Boleslaw II of Poland, who later became a king, and Wladyslaw Herman), it is thought probable that she was Vladimir's daughter by the last marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casimir I of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Casimir also signed an alliance with Yaroslav I the Wise, the Prince of Kievan Rus'. The alliance was sealed by Casimir's marriage with Yaroslav's sister, Maria Dobronega. With such support Casimir returned to Poland and managed t
2 CONC o retake most of his domain. In 1041, the defeated Bretislaus signed a treaty at Regensburg in which he renounced his claims to all Polish lands except for Silesia, which was to be incorporated into the Crown of Bohemia. It was Ca
2 CONC simir's success in strengthening royal power and ending internal strife that earned him the epithet of "the Restorer".
2 CONT
2 CONT Bolesław II the Bold
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Boleslaw was the eldest son of Casimir I the Restorer and Dobronega Maria of Kiev the daughter of the Grand Duke of Kiev Vladimir I.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Casimir I of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Casimir also signed an alliance with Yaroslav I the Wise, the Prince of Kievan Rus'. The alliance was sealed by Casimir's marriage with Yaroslav's sister, Maria Dobronega.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT MARRIAGE: Another marriage, following the death of Anne (1011), affiliated Vladimir with the Holy Roman emperors of the German Ottonian dynasty and produced a daughter, who became the consort of Casimir I the Restorer of Poland (1
2 CONC 016-58). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of St. Vladimir I, Grand Duke of Kiev.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT En mi nuevo libro LA SORPRENDENTE GENEALOGÍA DE MIS TATARABUELOS, encontrarán a este y muchos otros de sus ancestros con un resumen biográfico de cada uno. El libro está disponible en: amazon.com            barnesandnoble.com     
2 CONC         palibrio.com.  Les será de mucha utilidad y diversión.  Ramón Rionda
2 CONT
2 CONT In my new book LA SORPRENDENTE GENEALOGÍA DE MIS TATARABUELOS, you will find this and many other of your ancestors, with a biography summary of each of them. The book is now available at:  amazon.com            barnesandnoble.com 
2 CONC             palibrio.com.  Check it up, it’s worth it. Ramón Rionda
