3 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/22/cf/5e/ea/5344485d857efe6d/46d17f70-d56b-4a7d-9eba-1bfbfafb401d_original.jpg?hash=66391248da331c90f9bf6c9329c47ece66e68e3f15e9143d317b2bc160221a02.1794038399
3 FORM jpg
3 TITL Vsevolod’s wife
3 NOTE And why is it written MO.ACHE? The punctuation would indicate a shortening of a word. If it was to indicate the position of a nun in should and could have been written MONACHA.
3 NOTE The reasoning of Khazdan doesn't really hold. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Greek root: μοναχός (monakos, single solitary, μόνος monos,  = alone
4 CONT
4 CONT Latin: 
4 CONT       	monachus = monk, (vocative would be monache. i.e. be a monk)
4 CONT         monacha = nun       (genitive would be monachae. i.e. the nun's)
4 CONT
4 CONT Did latin come in different dialects, written differently on seals? Sigillographers would know.
