2 CONC  one should be chosen king who was of the royal race"[360].  If his parentage is as shown here, he must have been very old at the time.  In another passage, Snorre names "Nikolas…a son of Sigurd Hranason and of Skialdvor, a daught
2 CONC er of Brynjolf Ulfalde, and a sister of Haldor Brynjolfson by the father's side, and of King Magnus Barefoot by the mother's side", recording that he "had a farm at Ongul in Halogaland…called Steig" and "a house in Nidaros, below 
2 CONC St Jon's church, where Thorgeir the scribe lately dwelt"[361].  Snorre records that he was killed fighting the Birkebeins[362].  '''married  ?.   The name of Nikolas's wife is not known.'''  
