1 NOTE Kenneth II of Scotland
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=c9592d47-2fd3-45a6-9030-c4a3d6ab3f9b&tid=9784512&pid=-559741414
1 NOTE OR "CINAID"; KING OF SCOTS 971-995; KILLED BY HIS OWN MEN
1 NOTE 32nd great grandfather
1 NOTE
2 CONT King of Alba
2 CONT Reigned from 871 to 995. Succeeded by his cousin Constantine III. {Burke�s Peerage} [GADD.GED]
2 CONT Killed on behalf of his moray Cousin and successor
1 NOTE He began his reign by ravaging the Britons, probably as an act of vengeance, but his name is also included among a group of northern and western kings said to have made submission to the Anglo-Saxon king Edgar in 973, perhaps at C
2 CONC hester; and the chronicler Roger of Wendover (Flores Historiarum, under the year 975) states that shortly afterward Kenneth received from Edgar all the land called Lothian (i.e., between the Tweed and the Forth rivers). This is th
2 CONC e first mention of the River Tweed as the recognized border between England and Scotland. Kenneth was slain, apparently by his own subjects, at Fettercairn in the Mearns.
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded: King of the united Picts and Scots, 971.
