2 CONT RAGNHILD Magnusdatter.  Morkinskinna records that King Magnus´s daughter “Ragnhildr” was “no more than a child” when her father died[272].  Snorre records the marriage of "Hakon Ivarson" and "Ragnhild [daughter of] King Magnus"[27
2 CONC 3].  Morkinskinna records that “Hákon” as son of “Ívarr hvíti” married “King Magnus´s daughter Ragnhildr”, dated to [1062] from the context[274].  m ([1062]) HAAKON Ivarsson Jarl of the Uplands in Norway, son of IVAR Hvide & his w
2 CONC ife --- (-after 1065). 
