2 TITL Henry Of Burgundy (1066 - 1112) - Find A Grave Memorial
1 NOTE
2 CONT from &quot;Our Folk&quot; by Albert D Hart, Jr.
1 NOTE Henry I of Burgundy, Count of Portugal, Crusader in Spain. [Royalty forCommoners, 3rd ed., R. W. Stuart, Genealogical Publishing County,Baltimore, MD, 1998]
2 CONT
2 CONT When the African Almoravids annexed Muslim Spain, Alfonso VI of León(1065-1109) and Castile (1072-1109) provided for the defense of the westby calling on Henry, brother of Duke Eudes (Odo) of Burgundy, whom hemarried to his illegi
2 CONC timate daughter Teresa and made count of Portugal.From 1095, therefore, Henry and Teresa (who used the title of queen)ruled Portugal and Coimbra. On the death of Alfonso VI, his realms passedto his legitimate daughter Urraca and h
2 CONC er little son Alfonso (VII). Henryof Portugal sought power but had achieved little when he died in 1112,leaving Teresa with an infant son, Afonso Henriques. Teresa's intrigueswith her Galician favourite, Fernando Peres of Trava, l
2 CONC ost her thesupport of the Portuguese barons, and in 1128 followers of her sondefeated and drove her into exile. [Encyclopaedia Britannica CD '97]
