2 CONT ==[https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poppo_II,_Margrave_of_Carniola Poppo II, Margrave of Carniola, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Poppo II (died 1098), Count of Weimar-Orlamünde, was margrave of Carniola from 1070 and of Istria from 1096 to his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Richgard (lt: Richardis), daughter of Count Engelbert of Sponheim (de), who governed Istria until his death on 1 April 1096. According to the 1170 Historia Welforum chronicle, Poppo and Richgard had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sophia of Istria (d. 1132), married Count Berthold II of Andechs, mother of Margrave Berthold I of Istria (1110/1122–1188)
2 CONT * Hedwig, married firstly Count Herman I of Winzenburg and secondly Count Adalbert II of Bogen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Poppo remained a loyal supporter of the Salian emperor Henry IV during the Investiture Controversy. Because of his lack of surviving sons, he was succeeded by his younger brother Ulric II.
2 CONT
