2 CONT
2 CONT WIKIPEDIA (Eng)
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin V of Flanders (died 1 September 1067) was Count of Flanders from 1035 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Baldwin IV, Count of Flanders, who died in 1035.
2 CONT
2 CONT History
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1028 Baldwin married Adèle of France in Amiens, daughter of King Robert II of France; at her instigation he rebelled against his father but in 1030 peace was sworn and the old count continued to rule until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT During a long war (1046–1056) as an ally of Godfrey the Bearded, Duke of Lorraine, against the Holy Roman Emperor Henry III, he initially lost Valenciennes to Hermann of Hainaut. However, when the latter died in 1051 Baldwin marri
2 CONC ed his son Baldwin VI to Herman's widow Richildis and arranged that the sons of her first marriage were disinherited, thus de facto uniting the County of Hainaut with Flanders. Upon the death of Henry III this marriage was acknowl
2 CONC edged by treaty by Agnes de Poitou, mother and regent of Henry IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1060 to 1067 Baldwin was the co-Regent with Anne of Kiev for his nephew-by-marriage Philip I of France, indicating the importance he had acquired in international politics.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin and Adèle had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Baldwin VI, 1030-1070
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Matilda, c.1031-1083 who married William the Conqueror
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert I of Flanders, c.1033–1093
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry of Flanders c.1035
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sir Richard of Flanders c. 1050-1105
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Tanner, Heather J, Families, Friends and Allies: Boulogne and Politics in Northern France and England, C.879-1160
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT DISAMBIGUATION
2 CONT
2 CONT As for anyone coming across these lines: there are MANY different Baudouin de Flandre (Baldwin of Flanders):
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin I Iron Arm (r. 860s-879), married Judith and was granted lands and honours, which would evolve into the County of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin II the Bald (r. 879-918), son of Baldwin I and Judith
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arnulf I the Great (r. 918-964), son of Baldwin II, joinly with:
2 CONT
2 CONT o Baldwin III (r. 958-962), son of Arnulf I
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arnulf II (r. 964-988), son of Baldwin III
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin IV the Bearded (r. 988-1037), son of Arnulf II, father of Judith who married Tostig Godwinsson
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin V of Lille (r. 1037-1067), son of Baldwin IV, father of Mathilda (Maud) married to William Conqueror
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin VI (r. 1067-1070), son of Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arnulf III (r. 1070-1071), son of Baldwin VI, Count of Hainaut
2 CONT
2 CONT * Robert I the Frisian (r. 1071-1093), son of Baldwin VI
2 CONT
2 CONT * Robert II (r. 1093-1111), son of Robert I
2 CONT
2 CONT * Baldwin VII Hapkin (r. 1111-1119), son of Robert II
2 CONT
