2 CONT
2 CONT ES II:5 gives only one wife to Baldwin namely Adelaide of France widow of
2 CONT Richard III of Normandie.[FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Also called Baldwin of Lille, French Baudouin De Lille, DutchBoudewijn Van Rijsel count of Flanders who became one of the mostinfluential figures of 11th-century Europe. He was an active,enterprising man and greatly extended hi
2 CONC s power by wars and alliances. Heobtained from the Holy Roman emperor Henry IV the territory between theScheldt and the Dender as an imperial fief, as well as the margravate ofAntwerp. So powerful had he become that on the decease
2 CONC  of Henry I ofFrance he was appointed regent during the minority of Philip I (1060–66).Before his death he saw his eldest daughter Matilda (d. 1083) sharing theEnglish throne with William the Conqueror; saw his eldest son, Baldwin
2 CONC  ofMons, in possession of Hainaut in right of his wife Richilde, heiress ofRegnier V (d. 1036); and saw his second son, Robert the Frisian, regent(voogd) of the county of Holland.
2 CONT
2 CONT To cite this page: "Baldwin V" Encyclopædia Britannica
2 CONT  <http://www.britannica.com/eb/article?idxref=190720>Ancestral FileNumber:<AFN> 8XJK-Z6
