2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berthold_I._(Z%C3%A4hringen)
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold war in erster Ehe mit '''Richwara''' verheiratet, Tochter von Herzog [https://www.geni.com/people/Konrad-II-of-Carinthia/6000000035970859947 Konrad II. von Kärnten]. Die beiden hatten fünf bekannte Kinder:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Hermann I., Begründer der Linie der Markgrafen von Baden
2 CONT *Luitgard * um 1047, ⚭ Diepold II. im Thurgau, Markgraf im Nordgau *1033, † 7. August 1078
2 CONT *Richinza von Spitzenberg, 1. ⚭ H. von Frickingen, 2. ⚭ Ludwig von Sigmaringen
2 CONT *Berthold II., Herzog von Schwaben, später von Zähringen
2 CONT *Gebhard III., Bischof von Konstanz
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Richwara, possibly a descendant of Duke [https://www.geni.com/people/Konrad-II-of-Carinthia/6000000035970859947 Conrad II of Carinthia]  
2 CONT The couple had at least three sons: Herman I (c. 1040 – 1074), inherited the Veronese margravial title and became progenitor of the Margraves of Baden Berthold II (c. 1050 – 1111), Duke of Swabia in opposition to Frederick from Ho
2 CONC henstaufen from 1092 to 1098 Gebhard (c. 1050 – 1110), Bishop of Constance from 1084.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richwara also gave birth to two daughters: Liutgard (d. about 1119), married the Nordgau margrave Diepold of Vohburg, mother of Margrave Diepold III and grandmother of Adelaide of Vohburg, the first wife of Emperor Frederick Barba
2 CONC rossa Richinza, married Count Rudolf of Frickingen, secondly married to Louis of Sigmaringen, progenitor of the House of Helfenstein.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berthold_II,_Duke_of_Carinthia ''[draft]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SWABIA.htm#HermannIVSwabiadied1038
2 CONT
2 CONT a)       '''  [RICHWARA''' (-before 1056).  According to Wegener, Richwara wife of Berthold [I] [von Zähringen] was the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Herman-IV-duke-of-Swabia/6000000006906550197 Hermann IV Duke of Swabi
2 CONC a][221].  '''However, this seems unlikely from a chronological point of view.'''  Richwara gave birth to five children, presumably between [1045/55], so is unlikely to have been born later than 1030, when her supposed father was o
2 CONC nly 15 years old and her supposed mother about 10.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as his first wife, BERTHOLD I von Zähringen, son of BEZZELIN von Villingen & his wife [Luitgard ---] (-Limburg 5/6 Nov 1078, bur Hirsau).  Duke of Carinthia 1061.  Marchese di Verona 1066.''']'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BADEN.htm#Berchtolddied1078
2 CONT
2 CONT ''a)         BERTHOLD (-Limburg 5/6 Nov 1078, bur Hirsau).  .. ... ....''
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly '''RICHWARA''', daughter of --- (-before [1056]).  .  The wife of "Berchtoldus dux de Zaringen" is named "Richwara" in a list of founders of the monastery of St Peter in Schwarzwald[32].  According to Wegener, she was Ri
2 CONC chwara of Swabia, daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Herman-IV-duke-of-Swabia/6000000006906550197 Hermann IV Duke of Swabia] [Babenberg] & his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Adelaide-di-Susa/4957925920090125485   Adelaida
2 CONC  di Susa].  '''However, this seems unlikely from a chronological point of view.'''  Richwara gave birth to five children, presumably between [1045/55], so is unlikely to have been born later than 1030, when her supposed father was
2 CONC  only 15 years old and her supposed mother about 10.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ''m secondly ([1056]) BEATRIX de Mousson, daughter of LOUIS Comte de Mousson & his wife Sophie of Upper Lotharingia  (-26 Oct 1092, bur Toul Cathedral).  ..''
2 CONT
2 CONT   Duke Berthold & his first wife had five children:
