1 CONC air II in 1135. Boleslaw sent missionaries into Pomerania, converted the pagan tribes there to Christianity, and integrated the people into the Polish state. He then enacted legislation tosecure Pomerania and Silesia for his eldes
1 CONC t son and lesser provinces for his younger sons. The senioriate system, a halfway measure betweenprimogeniture and equal distribution among all male heirs, was devised to satisfy all princely heirs; yet it caused dissension and ev
