0 @N6000000002187982344@ NOTE Erling Skjalgson married King Olaf Trygveson's sister Astrid in summer and a great many people were assembled at it. King Olaf was also there, and offered Erling an earldom. Erling replied thus: "All my relations have been herses 
1 CONC only, and I will take no higher title than they have; but this I will accept from thee, King, that thou makest me the greatest of that title in the country." The king consented; and at his departure the king invested his brother-i
1 CONC n-law Erling with all the land north of the Sognefjord, and east to the Lidandisnes, on the same terms as Harald Harfager had given land to his sons.
1 CONT When Harald Gormson, king of Denmark, had adopted Christianity, he sent a message over all his kingdom that all people should be baptized, and converted to the true faith. He himself followed his message, and used power and violen
1 CONC ce where nothing else would do. He sent two erls, Urguthrjot and Brimilskjar, with many people to Norway, to proclaim Christianity there. In Viken, which stood directly under the king's power, this succeeded, and many were baptize
1 CONC d of the country folk. But when Svein Forkedbeard, immediately after his father King Harald's death, went out on war expeditions in Saxland, Frisland, and at last in England, the Northmen who had taken up Christianity returned bac
1 CONC k to heathen sacrifices, just as before; and the people in the north of the country did the same. . [Heimskringla: The Chronicle of the Kings of Norway - King Olaf Trygvason's Saga: Part II, chap. 64]
0 @N6000000003949916142@ NOTE King Olaf went with his men-at-arms to the Gula-Thing; for the bondes had sent him word that they would reply there to his speech. When both parties had come to the Thing, the king desired first to have a conference with the chief
1 CONC  people of the country; and when the meeting was numerous the king set forth his errand, -- that he desired them, according to his proposal, to allow themselves to be baptized. Then said Olmod the Old, " We relations have consider
1 CONC ed together this matter, and have come to one resolution. If thou thinkest, king, to force us who are related together to such things as to break our old law, or to bring us under thyself by any sort of violence, then will we stan
1 CONC d against thee with all our might: and be the victory to him to whom fate ordains it. But if thou, king, wilt advance our relations' fortunes, then thou shalt have leave to do as thou desirest, and we will all serve thee with zeal
1 CONC  in thy purpose."
1 CONT The king replies, " What do you propose for obtaining this agreement?"
1 CONT Then answers Olmod, " The first is, that thou wilt give thy sister Astrid in marriage to Erling Skjalgson, our relation, whom we look upon as the most hopeful young man in all Norway."
1 CONT King Olaf replied, that this marriage appeared to him also very suitable; "as Erling is a man of good birth, and a good-looking man in appearance: but Astrid herself must answer to this proposal."
1 CONT Thereupon the king spoke to his sister. She said, " It is but of little use that I am a king's sister, and a king~s daughter, if I must marry a man who has no high dignity or office. I will rather wait a few years for a better mat
1 CONC ch." Thus ended this conference.
1 CONT 63. HORDALAND BAPTIZED.
1 CONT King Olaf took a falcon that belonged to Astrid, plucked off all its feathers, and then sent it to her. Then said Astrid, " Angry is my brother." And she stood up, and went to the king, who received her kindly, and she said that s
1 CONC he left it to the king to determine her marriage. "I think, " said the king, " that I must have power enough in this land to raise any man I please to high dignity." Then the king ordered Olmod and Erling to be called to a confere
1 CONC nce, and all their relations; and the marriage was determined upon, and Astrid betrothed to Erling. Thereafter the king held the Thing, and recommended Christianity to the bondes; and as Olmod, and Erling, and all their relations,
1 CONC  took upon themselves the most active part in forwarding the king's desire, nobody dared to speak against it; and all the people were baptized, and adopted Christianity.
1 CONT 64. ERLING SKJALGSON'S WEDDING.
1 CONT Erling Skjalgson had his wedding in summer, and a great many people were assembled at it. King Olaf was also there, and offered Erling an earldom. Erling replied thus: "All my relations have been herses only, and I will take no hi
1 CONC gher title than they have; but this I will accept from thee, king, that thou makest me the greatest of that title in the country." The king consented; and at his departure the king invested his brother-in law Erling with all the l
1 CONC and north of the Sognefjord, and east to the Lidandisnes, on the same terms as Harald Harfager had given land to his sons, as before related.
0 @N6000000005561621733@ NOTE Mektig herse over landet fra Sognefjord til Lindesnes. Med kong Olav Trygvessøn på toget til Vendland, Erling den gjeveste av alle lendermenn i Norge, førte et stort hus med mange menn i sin tjeneste, såvel hjemme som i hærferd, k
1 CONC jempet til en begynnelse mot Olav Haraldssøn, men etler slaget ved Nesjar kom en utsoning i stand, hvorunder Erling måtte gi avkall på en del av sine len, senere brudd mellem ham og kongen, Erling reiste til kong Knud i England og
1 CONC  prøvet å overrumple kongen da han kom hjem, da denne skulde fare fra Viken til Trondheim, men Erling uheldig og selv overrumplet, i en trefning ved Tungeøene Erling overvunnet og måtte overgi sig, men kongen hånet ham og han blev
1 CONC  drept av sin frende og fiende Aslak Fitjaskalle, dette skjebnesvangert for kongen.
0 @N6000000007255394343@ NOTE [Londal.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT På Sola står en bautastein over Erling Skjalgson. Den ble avduket 1. juli 1934 av kong Håkon 7.
1 CONT Fremsiden: Erling Skjalgson + symbolene kornaks, spade og sverd.
1 CONT Baksiden: Arbeid - truskap - fridom.
1 CONT Bautaen er reist av folk på Sola gard i 1934.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kirken som det enda er ruiner etter ble trolig bygd av han.
1 CONT Nede ved Hafrsfjord er det synlige tufter etter store skipsnaust.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kong Olav sa til Erlings banemann: "No hogg du Noreg av mine hender".
0 @N6000000000944947441@ NOTE Konge. Død ca. 1066. 
1 CONT Konge av Sverige 1061 - 1066.
1 CONT Stenkilslekten etterfulgte Munsöslekten som konger av Sverige fra 1056 til 1125. Slekten ble etterfulgt av Sverkerslekten og Erikslekten.
1 CONT Stenkil var i slekt med den gamle kongeætten, og ble konge etter at Emund Slemme døde i 1060. Han arbeidet ivrig for kristendommens utbredelse i Sverige. I motsetning til sine foretredere samarbeidet han med representanter for kir
1 CONC ken i Hamburg-Bremen, biskop Egino av Dalby og biskop Adalvard d.y. av Sigtuna. Stenkil forhindret den sistnevnte i å brenne ned hedningtemplet i Uppsala. Etter hans død utbrøt det en hednisk reaksjon i Sverige.
