0 @N6000000001744974526@ NOTE A major figure in British/Norse history. Became Earl of Northumberland in 1055 (at that time, most of East Coast of England). His cousin was King Swein of Denmark. In 1065 he was deposed by Northumbrians and went to Flanders. Brot
1 CONC her of King Harold Godwinson, whose reign he challenged with the aid of Norwegian King Harald Hardrade.  This brought about the demise of both men at the decisive Battle of Stamford Bridge in 1066.
1 CONT
1 CONT See Snorre Sturlason (1179-1241), Heimskringla or the Lives of the Norse Kings (NY: Dover, 1932, 1990)
