0 @N6000000002187592881@ NOTE Robert I, Count of Flanders
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I of Flanders (b. between 1029 and 1032 – October 13, 1093, Kassel), known as Robert the Frisian, was count of Flanders from 1070 to 1092.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the younger son of Baldwin V of Flanders and Adela Capet, a daughter of King Robert II of France.
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert was originally intended to secure the northern borders of Flanders by his marriage to Gertrude of Saxony, Dowager Countess of Holland, but after his brother's death in 1070 he displaced his nephews and became count of Fland
1 CONC ers.
1 CONT
1 CONT By Gertrude of Holland he had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Robert II
1 CONT     * Adela (d. 1115), who first married king Canute IV of Denmark, and was the mother of Charles the Good, later count of Flanders. She then married Roger Borsa, duke of Apulia.
1 CONT     * Gertrude, who married Thierry II, Duke of Lorraine, and was the mother of Thierry of Alsace, also later count of Flanders
1 CONT     * Philip of Loo, whose illegitimate son William of Ypres was also a claimant to the county of Flanders
1 CONT     * Ogiva, abbess of Messines
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Arnulf III Count of Flanders
1 CONT 1070–1092 Succeeded by
1 CONT Robert II
