1 CONT fought with the Bretons, Saxons, and Vikings while consolidating his kingdom
1 CONT
1 CONT His wife may have been a princess of leinster
1 CONT
1 CONT tradition says he was murdered at Fettercairn, Scotland by his own subjects through the intrigue of Finella (daughter of Cuncar Earl of Angus and wife of the Maormor of the Mearns) in revenge for her son being executed.  He was bu
1 CONC ried at Iona.
0 @N6000000006348204610@ NOTE Kenneth II (971-95)
1 CONT Kenneth was the brother of Dubh. In 973 he acknowledged King Edgar of England as his lord in return for recognition that the Scots now held Lothian, which they had seized from the Angles. In about 994, however, he broke his promis
1 CONC e to keep the peace and invaded England. He was defeated, and lost Lothian again. He killed Culen's brother in 977 and was himself killed in 995 in a blood feud at Fettercairn, Kincardineshire by Culen's son, Constantine.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source:  Official Website of the British Government
