0 @N6000000000945044284@ NOTE Sigurd var den siste småkongen i Norge. Han var konge på Opplandene, hadde 
1 CONT gårdsbruk på Ringerike og bodde etter et gammelt sagn på gården Bønsnes. Han skildres som
1 CONT en fredsommelig mann som best likte å stelle på gården. Derfor fikk ha navnet ?Syr?, dvs. so
1 CONT eller purke. Forøvrig var han forstandig, sindig og måteholden. Han hjalp sin stesønn Olav den
1 CONT Hellige til å vinne overherredømmet etter slaget ved Nesjar.
0 @N6000000002187914614@ NOTE Sigurd Syr
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Sigurd Syr Halfdansson (sometimes spelled "Halvdansson") (c. 970-1018) was a great-grandson of Harald I of Norway. He was subking of Ringerike, an ancient territory in the county of Buskerud, southern Norway. Sigurd was stepfather
1 CONC  of King Olaf Haraldsson and father of Harald III of Norway.1
1 CONT
1 CONT Sigurd Syr was baptized into the Christian faith in 988. According to the Heimskringla, "...King Olaf Trygvason came to Ringerike to spread Christianity, Sigurd Syr and his wife allowed themselves to be baptized..."2,3
1 CONT
1 CONT His nickname Syr means "sow", and was not complementary.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sigurd Syr was a prudent man, taciturn and generally modest, although very wealthy. He was known as a good caretaker of his peoples' businesses, personally involved in their oversight, and he was knowledgeable about the local Norw
1 CONC egian economy. He was not fond of the pomp and ceremony of nobility, but participated in his role.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sigurd Syr wasn't personally very ambitious, but he fully supported his stepson, King Olaf Haraldsson's ambitions of leadership and command. In 1014, he successfully petitioned his peers, the other Norwegian district Kings, to gar
1 CONC ner their support for a new war against Sweden, Denmark and England that commenced in 1015. This war was his stepson's cause.
1 CONT
1 CONT 13th century historian and mythographer Snorri Sturluson is the author of the Heimskringla, the source of the information currently documented in this article.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Note 1: Sigurd "Syr" King of Ringerike geneology entry at american-pictures.com retrieved Sept 12, 2005
1 CONT     * Note 2: Wikisource text King Olaf Trygvason's Saga, Part II, "Section 24, Olaf Haraldson Baptized"
1 CONT     * Note 3: World Wide School Heimskringla - Norwegian Kings - Vol. 3 Book V, Chapter 67, by Snorri Sturlson [sic] at www.worldwideschool.org
1 CONT
1 CONT (Norway)
